iv> </div> </div><br /> Are you kidding? That entire concept is <u><i><b>fucking horrifying</b></i></u>.<br /> <br /> You can play as a Demigod in Exalted because <i><u><b>there are no real people in Creation</b></u></i>. It is <i>literally</i> &quot;make-believe&quot;. When your Exalt goes into Limit Break and fuckmurders a city in their rage, you shrug <i>because the thousands of &quot;people&quot; that just got &quot;murdered&quot;</i><i><b>aren't real</b></i>.<br /> <br /> Debating someone so charismatic as to effectively have <i>mind control</i> would not be awesome. Trying to stop a demigod as they rage their way through the subway wouldn't be cool. Not being able to trust if your friends or family are <i>actually who they say they are</i> would not be a pleasant experience. <br /> <br /> Just because the Exalted are &quot;heroic&quot; in the Classical sense of the term <i><b><u>does not</u></b></i> mean they are nice people, or good people, or even kinda-sorta decent people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","user":"Boston123","date":". 10-27-2019, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T18:27:48-07:00","id":1344105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344101#post1344101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Are you kidding? That entire concept is <u><i><b>fucking horrifying</b></i></u>.<br /> <br /> You can play as a Demigod in Exalted because <i><u><b>there are no real people in Creation</b></u></i>. It is <i>literally</i> &amp;quot;make-believe&amp;quot;. When your Exalt goes into Limit Break and fuckmurders a city in their rage, you shrug <i>because the thousands of &amp;quot;people&amp;quot; that just got &amp;quot;murdered&amp;quot;</i><i><b>aren't real</b></i>.<br /> <br /> Debating someone so charismatic as to effectively have <i>mind control</i> would not be awesome. Trying to stop a demigod as they rage their way through the subway wouldn't be cool. Not being able to trust if your friends or family are <i>actually who they say they are</i> would not be a pleasant experience. <br /> <br /> Just because the Exalted are &amp;quot;heroic&amp;quot; in the Classical sense of the term <i><b><u>does not</u></b></i> mean they are nice people, or good people, or even kinda-sorta decent people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am perfectly aware of how horrifying exalts are when facing down mortals. Thank you very much. <br /> <br /> I still think it would be a pretty fun storyline. And a sight to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T22:17:44-07:00","id":1344127,"title":"","content":"Real life isn\u2019t storylines, Accelerator. There\u2019s no Storyteller carefully pulling strings to bring about an entertaining and coherent story so as to give the players a good time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-28-2019, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T23:22:05-07:00","id":1344137,"title":"","content":"Jesus Christ Accelerator is just giving an example of how Exalted Modern is a fun setting, stop interpreting literally everything he posts in the worst possible light. You all realize The World of Darkness and Chronicles of Darkness are a thing right? They are published and share writers with Exalted and use the premise of Supernaturals in our world?<br /> <br /> Do people honestly think Accelerator is advocating that you give reality warping powers to a bunch of Randos in the real world? He has gone off in threads where he has stated that he believes the creation of Exalted was the biggest mistake for Creation because of the horrors they have and can commit.<br /> <br /> People need to stop looking for pointless internet fights just because they believe they can get away with starting one in hopes punishing others who are just randos on the internet.<br /> <br /> Its childish, this is the toxic behavior I have complained about here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T23:23:12-07:00","id":1344138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344083#post1344083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Community but with Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Dan Hamon, take all my money</div> </div> </div> </div>My first Chuubo Game I wanted to run was essentially using Chuubo's Marvelous Wish Granting Engine to play in Greendale!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T23:46:42-07:00","id":1344142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344138#post1344138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first Chuubo Game I wanted to run was essentially using Chuubo's Marvelous Wish Granting Engine to play in Greendale!</div> </div> </div> </div>I have zero experience with Chuubo, but that sounds wonderful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T23:54:05-07:00","id":1344143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344142#post1344142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have zero experience with Chuubo, but that sounds wonderful.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I first read it I was like holy Crap I could literally use this system to play a tabletop game of anything from Harvest Moon to Rugrats, to Community, to Marvel Superheroes! Its a diceless system that actually makes a framework where story and drama and slice of life matters and is fun. I plan to sometime make a segway in an Exalted game where the Circle winds up in the Wyld and I will use the Chuubo rules to represent a sort of minigames arch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T23:54:24-07:00","id":1344144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344137#post1344137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus Christ Accelerator is just giving an example of how Exalted Modern is a fun setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>He did not. Exalted Modern does not have a North Korea. It's not our world; that's <i>why</i> it's a fun setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344137#post1344137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You all realize The World of Darkness and Chronicles of Darkness are a thing right? They are published and share writers with Exalted and use the premise of Supernaturals in our world?</div> </div> </div> </div>The world of the World of Darkness is a world that looks like our world, but has always had supernaturals walking in it and shaping its events. That's a pretty critical difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344137#post1344137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people honestly think Accelerator is advocating that you give reality warping powers to a bunch of Randos in the real world?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>He </i>sure seems to think so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344105#post1344105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think it would be a pretty fun storyline. And a sight to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-28-2019, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T04:03:13-07:00","id":1344163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344143#post1344143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I first read it I was like holy Crap I could literally use this system to play a tabletop game of anything from Harvest Moon to Rugrats, to Community, to Marvel Superheroes! Its a diceless system that actually makes a framework where story and drama and slice of life matters and is fun. I plan to sometime make a segway in an Exalted game where the Circle winds up in the Wyld and I will use the Chuubo rules to represent a sort of minigames arch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mmmm. I really like slice of life (all my games, from Exalted to freaking Unknown Armies, always have a big slice of life component. And heck, I loved Golden Sky Stories when we played it), and this sounds pretty interesting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T05:10:50-07:00","id":1344169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344137#post1344137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus Christ Accelerator is just giving an example of how Exalted Modern is a fun setting, stop interpreting literally everything he posts in the worst possible light. You all realize The World of Darkness and Chronicles of Darkness are a thing right? They are published and share writers with Exalted and use the premise of Supernaturals in our world?<br /> <br /> Do people honestly think Accelerator is advocating that you give reality warping powers to a bunch of Randos in the real world? He has gone off in threads where he has stated that he believes the creation of Exalted was the biggest mistake for Creation because of the horrors they have and can commit.<br /> <br /> People need to stop looking for pointless internet fights just because they believe they can get away with starting one in hopes punishing others who are just randos on the internet.<br /> <br /> Its childish, this is the toxic behavior I have complained about here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I'm afraid you're wrong here, eldagusto. I kinda am advocating that. <br /> <br /> Mind you, I did mean 'interesting in the Chinese sense'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T15:37:46-07:00","id":1344274,"title":"","content":"Then I retract my sentiments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T15:44:54-07:00","id":1344276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344274#post1344274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I retract my sentiments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mighty big of you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T16:01:22-07:00","id":1344286,"title":"","content":"Anyway, back on the exaltation. I always liked the idea of putting exalted in more... Brutish settings. Just so I can watch them kick ass. Not just solars. Infernals, too. <br /> <br /> For example, Berserk. An infernal exaltation for either Guts or Griffith would be a thing. <br /> <br /> Or maybe 700 exaltations falling upon Laundry Files earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T17:38:23-07:00","id":1344303,"title":"","content":"Exalted upset the balance of power in any other fiction by virtue of being POWER. And the way they change the world is personal because Exalted is about Power and Choices. When you take the idea of an exalted 'shard' and throw it in to another world you are basically asking, &quot;If a person in this world was granted POWER, what would change?&quot; and while you can making sweeping generalizations such as &quot;Mighty oppressive empire A is gonna be destroyed fast from a Solar peasant revolt&quot; it is just as likely &quot;Leader of Mighty oppressive empire A is now a Solar leader.&quot; which would have drastically different endings for everyone. In a handful of settings, Exalted are just other strong players, but in no other world are they ignored or powerless. The other question about moving Exalted to other fictions is about rules. Most important to me is who can Exalt. Solars are intended to be Human excellence. Are Solar's not a thing is fictions without humans? Lunars are shapeshifters. They are more fluid for setting, but some settings have so many shapeshifters a Lunar might not stand out or be as impressive. But can a shape shifting creature exalt as a Lunar? What changes then? Dragon blooded are about family and the elements. Are there more dragonblooded in fictions with more elements? Can they fully convert? Can you have 8 elements and none of them fire, earth, air, wood, or water and still call them Dragon blooded? Can God's in other fictions suddenly burn themselves out and create Exigents? Do the dead start rising as hungry ghost if ghost never existed before? Do Abyssals bring death to a deathless world? What is a Green sun prince in a world with no concept of 'Yozi'? <br /> <br /> If you want amazing and exceptional people in other fictions, they are called Main Characters. If you want them filled with Solar power, they imagine they can reach their goals and then sail past them, and how that power changes them and the world around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T18:33:30-07:00","id":1344313,"title":"","content":"Fun fact of what I like about solars. <br /> <br /> They are never obsolete. <br /> <br /> Think of a man with super-strength. In some world's he's awesome. In others, he's not. Let's say this is conan the barbarian. A man with superstrength can cut down demons, men, tear down castle walls, and smash apart sorcerers. In a place like star wars, where superstrength won't help you pilot a starship or navigate politics, the strongman finds that he cannot apply his talents and in this regard is like any other human. Same for things like a mind reader or a teleporter or someone who can throw fire. All of them one-trick ponies. Ridiculously strong in one portion, but often lacking in other things. And when that one gift of theirs is rendered obsolete or bypassed, they're not really all that powerful or have great agency. <br /> <br /> I can't think of any situation where someone Exalting as a solar is competely useless. The Road, a book where an ecological disaster causes the destruction of human civilisation and majority of plant life, can be dealt with by a solar with exp in survival, occult, craft, socialize, and bureaucracy. Survival to gather food in insanely harsh conditions, and understand how to farm and grow crops. Occult for that sweet, sweet, sorcery (food from the aerial table and elemental summoning). Craft for creating farmhouses, generators, and greenhouses. Bureaucracy and socialize for gathering the survivors and putting them to work in vast underground warrens where they will survive whatever shit wiped out the ecosystem. And then occult and survival charms working together to form a celestial-scale working where the weather is balmy, the sun is shining, and there is green grass in an area the size of a city. Ta-dah, dodged. <br /> <br /> Or, say, star wars. A place where a bureaucracy or war-supernal can stride across the galaxy and shaking kings from their thrones. Or a story like 'A roadside picnic' where a craft or lore supernal would find the entire place to be a dream come true. Or Independence day, where one of the fighter pilots exalt as they fight off the mothership, archery charms channeled into his weaponry and drive charms into his plane. <br /> <br /> Thus I vote that solars should be put into a setting where they're most needed. Where there is something on that is stomping on the face of the human race, just like in primordial times. <br /> <br /> I say we put them in Vilcabamba. Or Crossed. Or the","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T01:02:24-07:00","id":1344360,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Conan isn't really a &quot;superstrength and that's all I've got&quot; hero though. Drop him into Star Wars and I can't see him becoming less than Klingon Han Solo. Assuming the most deferent crossover to Star Wars lore, rather than the version that defers to Conan's vibe, where he is *obviously* better at fighting and tactics than these guys with their cheap sorcery and hokey religion. That goes for quite a few heroes. One-magic trick heroes are pretty rare across media; even within superheroes where it's most applicable, it's more common to find a character with is a generally strong and capable hero with an extra schtick than a character who wholly depends on an ability.<br /> <br /> On Exalted flexibility, I'm less going to touch that as it really depends a lot on your assumptions and isn't really in the text. Does a person who is in his personality like modern day Demetheus become a genius scientist when he Dawn Exalts during an ecological collapse? I'm thinkin' no, but ultimately this is not a question you can find any answer on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T03:40:07-07:00","id":1344375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344313#post1344313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact of what I like about solars.<br /> <br /> They are never obsolete.<br /> <br /> Think of a man with super-strength. In some world's he's awesome. In others, he's not. Let's say this is conan the barbarian. A man with superstrength can cut down demons, men, tear down castle walls, and smash apart sorcerers. In a place like star wars, where superstrength won't help you pilot a starship or navigate politics, the strongman finds that he cannot apply his talents and in this regard is like any other human. Same for things like a mind reader or a teleporter or someone who can throw fire. All of them one-trick ponies. Ridiculously strong in one portion, but often lacking in other things. And when that one gift of theirs is rendered obsolete or bypassed, they're not really all that powerful or have great agency.<br /> <br /> I can't think of any situation where someone Exalting as a solar is competely useless. The Road, a book where an ecological disaster causes the destruction of human civilisation and majority of plant life, can be dealt with by a solar with exp in survival, occult, craft, socialize, and bureaucracy. Survival to gather food in insanely harsh conditions, and understand how to farm and grow crops. Occult for that sweet, sweet, sorcery (food from the aerial table and elemental summoning). Craft for creating farmhouses, generators, and greenhouses. Bureaucracy and socialize for gathering the survivors and putting them to work in vast underground warrens where they will survive whatever shit wiped out the ecosystem. And then occult and survival charms working together to form a celestial-scale working where the weather is balmy, the sun is shining, and there is green grass in an area the size of a city. Ta-dah, dodged.<br /> <br /> Or, say, star wars. A place where a bureaucracy or war-supernal can stride across the galaxy and shaking kings from their thrones. Or a story like 'A roadside picnic' where a craft or lore supernal would find the entire place to be a dream come true. Or Independence day, where one of the fighter pilots exalt as they fight off the mothership, archery charms channeled into his weaponry and drive charms into his plane.<br /> <br /> Thus I vote that solars should be put into a setting where they're most needed. Where there is something on that is stomping on the face of the human race, just like in primordial times.<br /> <br /> I say we put them in Vilcabamba. Or Crossed. Or the</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I agree with your exposition.<br /> <br /> Exceptionnal people in other settings aren't &quot;obsolete&quot;, because the life of these settings are driven by narrative stories we tell each others, not simulated real-life reconstruction. Look how many times people in Star Wars find themselves of someone who need to push a big rock or something out of their way with the Force.<br /> <br /> The only settings in which I could to some extent agree extraordinary people are osbolete are settings like the original Foundation from Asimov, because the point of these books are precisely that individuals do not matter because the course of history is determined by huge group behavior. And even then, some of his later books points to a refutal of these these ideas.<br /> <br /> Also I think you may need to be careful talking about political subjects on forums because it makes things weird for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T04:12:28-07:00","id":1344380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344375#post1344375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think I agree with your exposition.<br /> <br /> Exceptionnal people in other settings aren't &quot;obsolete&quot;, because the life of these settings are driven by narrative stories we tell each others, not simulated real-life reconstruction. Look how many times people in Star Wars find themselves of someone who need to push a big rock or something out of their way with the Force.<br /> <br /> The only settings in which I could to some extent agree extraordinary people are osbolete are settings like the original Foundation from Asimov, because the point of these books are precisely that individuals do not matter because the course of history is determined by huge group behavior. And even then, some of his later books points to a refutal of these these ideas.<br /> <br /> Also I think you may need to be careful talking about political subjects on forums because it makes things weird for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh wow. <br /> <br /> Hmm.... I disagree, though, in some way. I tend to look at it in a.... simulation? Not that narratively driven. I look at what a character has, and does, and uses, and put them into other settings and wonder how they'll do. I don't give them props just for being the main character. I give them props because they're smart, skilled, determined, and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T06:22:18-07:00","id":1344400,"title":"","content":"Yes I think I understand what you are trying to do.<br /> <br /> I thought like this for a long time before my opinion switched to what it is now, ie the opposite (which doesn't make me more &quot;right&quot; now than before, I just think differently).<br /> <br /> My main point for not agreeing to this point of view anymore is the following : Every simulation we can imagine is narratively driven, be it by characters, societal agendas or just themes. We could invent a thousand reasons for which extaordinary people put in another setting would be absolute rejects of society, a thousand different reasons for which they would become absolute god-like figures, and again another thousand reasons for which they would insert in society like any other individual and live a happy life. This is literally all what fiction is about : almost any book you can pick in sci-fi or fantasy or fictionnal or whatever section of a library or show on Netflix would give you explanation for this. Hell we even have this damn trend in anime called &quot;Isekai&quot; fed on us like crazy for 7 years or so that takes all aspect of this question and turn it upside down on all angles possibles and imaginable (well, from a certain Japanese angle at least I guess).<br /> <br /> Of course, you might say, others authors might have an approach that is biased in order to simulate a realistic situation, and my approach is more logical/objective/scientific than theirs. And obviously, this is not true. Because first, we have absolutely zero empirical methodology in order to attain this, because we do not have (and I suspect we will never have) enough computing power to calculate this simulation even if we had a model resulting from empirical methodology, and even if we had a model, we could not take into accounts many things that are not computable (say, free will, if you believe this kind of things exists). So in the end, wether you are willing to do it or not, your simulation is narratively driven by the arbitrary choices you decided to make to represent a reality that seems more grounded to you, but it's neither universal (different people might make different arbitrary choices) nor scientific.<br /> <br /> And honestly it's fine, I like your ideas of trying to put things in other settings, they are fun. I just don't agree with your interpretation that seems to imply there is an objective truth to some fictionnal characters being irrelevant in other settings and Solar not, because it relies on an assumption we can find some sort of objective reality to test it, and not one driven by narratives themes you arbitrary chose. An interpretation I agree with though, is why thematically it would not make sense for Solar Exalted to be irrelevant in any setting : They are usually presented as parangons of humanity, courage and valor. They are ususally presented as the force that can push humanity through the hardest times, even when all seems lost. A setting where they are irrelevant and obsolete would certainly be a very dark and cynical view on what humanity as a whole, I believe.<br /> <br /> Also it looks like I'm ranting on you or being very assertive in this post in which case I'm sorry because it's not the intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T08:49:47-07:00","id":1344424,"title":"","content":"Eh, I don't quite get what you're saying... but i respect it either way. I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T10:28:58-07:00","id":1344444,"title":"","content":"Basically my point is you can't make an objective simulation and you should rather come up with a thematic idea for the insertion of Exalted in a setting, not try to guess some random consequences you might come up with because then there is no theme for players or people to think about","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T11:31:27-07:00","id":1344455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344444#post1344444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically my point is you can't make an objective simulation and you should rather come up with a thematic idea for the insertion of Exalted in a setting, not try to guess some random consequences you might come up with because then there is no theme for players or people to think about</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, true. But I say that on fiction it would be best if what we wrote made sense and had logical consequences. I am of no love of the thought 'crazy enough to work' and other varieties. The main character can match a veteran in week's rather than years? There better be a reason for it. Same for underdogs defeating the overlord, and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T12:03:47-07:00","id":1344462,"title":"","content":"You're talking Exalted, yes a main character can match a veteran in weeks. I understand your concern for consistency but I think you need to be concerned with this : Many good stories have concistency, but all good stories have good themes. It should be your focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T12:14:05-07:00","id":1344467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344462#post1344462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're talking Exalted, yes a main character can match a veteran in weeks. I understand your concern for consistency but I think you need to be concerned with this : Many good stories have concistency, but all good stories have good themes. It should be your focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we are actually in agreement. <br /> <br /> What kind of themes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T12:32:46-07:00","id":1344473,"title":"","content":"I don't know, I can advise you to try reading some common themes and trying to figure out what would be interesting in a setting (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theme_(narrative)\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theme_(narrative)</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T12:40:35-07:00","id":1344477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344473#post1344473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, I can advise you to try reading some common themes and trying to figure out what would be interesting in a setting (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theme_(narrative)\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theme_(narrative)</a>)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nonono. <br /> <br /> You mentioned themes for exalted, right? Well, if you're throwing exaltation left and right into various settings, what themes would you bring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T12:51:33-07:00","id":1344480,"title":"","content":"Well I guess some core themes I would be interestted in would be legitimacy : In Exalted lots of characters have legitimacy because they have might or inherit some kind of legicimacy from greater sort of divine powers. Usually on earth this isn't the case, and I guess it could be a starting point : What is our relation to person wielding divine power, and why would we lend them political power (as people do in Exalted) ?<br /> <br /> I guess this sort of theme may already have numerous discussions in Comics books but I'm not an expert enough to know if this is true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T15:02:15-07:00","id":1344509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344480#post1344480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I guess some core themes I would be interestted in would be legitimacy : In Exalted lots of characters have legitimacy because they have might or inherit some kind of legicimacy from greater sort of divine powers. Usually on earth this isn't the case, and I guess it could be a starting point : What is our relation to person wielding divine power, and why would we lend them political power (as people do in Exalted) ?<br /> <br /> I guess this sort of theme may already have numerous discussions in Comics books but I'm not an expert enough to know if this is true.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. No. What legitimacy do they have? I mean, seriously. In Exalted, Divine Right means nothing. Divine Right means that the primordials, who, in case you haven't noticed, deliberately created humans to be crippled and weak are the ones in the right. Theion, righteouss psychotic jackass, is basically what Jehovah would be in real life if you stripped the blinders off. Divine right in exalted is bullshit. <br /> <br /> 2. We're on earth. We literally have no idea this is divine power. This could be aliens, psychic powers, ghosts, or hell, even the antichrist<br /> <br /> 3. Why would we lend them political power? <br /> <br /> Well, there is no why. Because it will come to them regardless. Think about it, for a moment. I'm literally writing about this right now, in another thread. Young girl, lower class, who barely has clothes on her back. She exalted in the midst of triumph as a medicine supernal. Several months later with several custom charms (and my own frankensteinish interpretation of the setting) she's currently selling priceless pieces of art, jewellery, and runs a back alley medical practice that far exceeds the success rate of entire fully stocked hospitals, because Solars, amirite? <br /> <br /> What happens when she goes public? Several things. They're going to be scared of her. And they're going to want her. Because she's literally giving out one of the most valuable thing in the world. Good health. And only she, can give it out. Imagine, say, a man with several thousand in his pocket and who's helplessly watching his mother descend into Alzheimers. How much will he pay? Or, say, a billionaire with with severe pancreatic cancer. How much will he pay, when chemotherapy and surgery has failed? <br /> <br /> How much power will she wield? <br /> <br /> And here's the thing. This applies for everything and anything a solar might do. A solar with dots in performance can literally sing on the roadside and become an instant sensation. A solar specialising in melee or range or combat can singlehandedly storm up to a dictator, behead him, and take over an entire nation. And let's not forget what an exalt with bureaucracy charms can do with the stock market. <br /> <br /> The funny thing about humanity and their elite is, is that we constantly try to pretend they're better. Look at Kim Jong Un's propaganda stories. Or the prosperity gospel of America. Or of all the bullshit spewed by nobles in medieval times. The cold hard truth is that, with rare exceptions, no man is irreplaceable. No matter who you are or what your title is, the cold hard truth is that if some random peasant was switched out with you (years of training and good nutrition) you will be replaced. Same goes for battle. It doesn't matter how good a fighter you are, being outnumbered 5 to 1 is enough to bring you down. <br /> <br /> Then enter the Exalted. <br /> <br /> An exalted appearing on earth would be catastrophic on frankly speaking, the very thought of equality. All men are equal.... except for this one. If the Exalt is smart or competent or lucky in any way, they can very likely grab the attentions of the masses and wield incredibly outsized influence. An exalt deciding to get into politics is someone that will very likely be runing the country within 10 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T08:06:09-07:00","id":1344664,"title":"","content":"In the time before record, in the blank vastness of prehis-<br /> tory, the gods of Heaven created champions to carry their<br /> power and glory, wage wars in their name, and fight the<br /> battles they never could. These heroic men and women<br /> were called the Exalted, for they had been uplifted. For<br /> their service, the gods gave the Exalted rule over all Cre-<br /> ation\u2014over all the peoples and the beasts and the spirits<br /> dwelling there. All the lands which they could see and<br /> grasp were theirs. Having done this, the gods of Heaven<br /> retired to Yu-Shan, the Celestial City, and left the world<br /> of man to the Exalted.<br /> <br /> From Exalted Core 3e page 21.<br /> <br /> There is a clear theme of legitimacy to rule upon the world and its people in Exalted.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate religion states Dragon-Blooded are natural rulers of the World. The Celestial Exalted are chosen by the mightiest of the Gods. You really should try to think about it.<br /> <br /> Also there are numerous interesting ideas in what you propose, for example : What is the price we are willing to pay for good health ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T08:12:30-07:00","id":1344665,"title":"","content":"A lot. Look at how much money is paid to conmen, for assortef bullshit. Like bleach enemas, vitamins, fad diets, stem cell crap, faith healing, psychic powers. All to push away the spectre of death and things like cancer or multiple sclerosis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T08:21:18-07:00","id":1344666,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's a description, now try to to say something consistent about it. Something that speaks about the nature of the human heart, and you have a theme used well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T15:28:56-07:00","id":1344758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344509#post1344509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theion, righteouss psychotic jackass, is basically what Jehovah would be in real life if you stripped the blinders off.</div> </div> </div> </div>If by &quot;blinders&quot; you mean 99% of scripture, which provides evidence to the contrary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T16:19:59-07:00","id":1344768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344664#post1344664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There is a clear theme of legitimacy to rule upon the world and its people in Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of this theme is a deconstruction though; the Dragonblood's right to rule is based on a karmic system that (probably?) isn't true, the Solar are the rightful returning Kings, but why are they really rightful? (It's a bit Taergaryan-esque; they were usurped as the rightful rulers... except why were they rightful?) They usurped the previous rulers after all. In fact, is divine right (and Solars do, arguably, have Divine Right, being chosen by the Gods) really that rightful when the Gods themselves are imperfect?<br /> <br /> I mean, this is not to say that it's not an important theme of Exalted; it absolutely is! What makes legitimacy, who has legitimacy to rule, is a very key theme. But the theme isn't really exactly &quot;whose Divine Right is correct&quot;, that's just what the Solars and Dragonblood<i> think</i> is the theme of the story they're in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think you could use Exalted in the modern world as a look at religious legitimacy; messiahs and prophets with miraculous powers. Is this Solar the second coming of Jesus, the Antichrist, a Saint, or just a conmen using some kind of weird unknown tech to trick you into joining their cult?<br /> <br /> But you're basically introducing superheroes, and there's a reason that superhero stories generally don't revolve around the superheroes becoming the ruling <i>political</i> class (sometimes they do! But not generally). In our society, our idea of legitimacy is who best embodies the will of the people (expressed via voting), which doesn't really segue into super-skill. (Super-bureaucracy can help you maintain power via competence, but doesn't generally help you win power, as every candidate claims to be better at administration than the current guy. Super-presence and super-socialise is obviously very useful though, showing you can control your party.)<br /> <br /> If Britain suddenly got a Solar, I don't think anyone would argue that he/she should replace Elizabeth as our Queen. Nor that they should become Prime Minister, unless they get behind a programme of popular policies.<br /> (Obviously you can look into themes of what happens with a politician who can make people believe whatever they say, of course.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T16:23:00-07:00","id":1344769,"title":"","content":"So, what about Exaltations in Lovecraftian cosmic horror?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T16:33:49-07:00","id":1344772,"title":"","content":"Either the Solars punch Chtulu to death, deflating the entire setting. OR they fall and go mad like anyone else, in which case they become an absurd demonstration that literally no one stands a chance against cosmic horror, not even the most perfectest bestest champions ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T17:31:35-07:00","id":1344781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344758#post1344758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If by &quot;blinders&quot; you mean 99% of scripture, which provides evidence to the contrary.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if someone's nice to his chosen in-group <i>most </i>of the time (except when he gets mad, then all bets are off), but outside that group he actively promotes genocide against another people, is he a nice guy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T18:17:03-07:00","id":1344790,"title":"","content":"I remember making an outline for this. One thousand Exaltations falling onto Laundry Files Earth. <br /> <br /> Things get hairy. Exalted aren't powerful just because of charms. But because due to being Exalted, they are immune to the insanity and madness inflicting majority of lovecraftian magic practitioners, blasting off spells continuously and reliably when such an effort will leave mortal men gibbering in insanity, dead, without doing things like 'become an empire'. <br /> <br /> The Black Chamber tries to enslave them, as does the Laundry and others. Standard thing is to grab anyone with any true inkling of what's happenign and make sure they don't pop out anything, and give them busy work. Silence and obedience is kept through geas, basically slave marks and binding contracts. Which is... really bad. Considering that they actually leave the exalt alive. Which means that slowly, ever so slowly, the geas breaks and is shattered. Some organisations just fall. They're either wiped out by exalts who have already specialised in combat, destroyed by bureaucracy supernals, or just plain ass have the tables turned on them. Fun fact about magic in The Laundry Files. It's basically coding and programming, and exalted being exalted, they can learn, program, and code along with the best of them, inflicting and unwinding the geas like a piece of cloth with a string on it. <br /> <br /> So now standard organisation protocol is to either run, flee, or fight them. Talking is right out, after they begin talking to socialized-specced and realize that yes, they should join it. Case Nightmare Green is on the way, when the walls of reality turn thin and abominations from beyond time and space enter our earth to eat our souls. There is no way to survive. The only solutions are to cast off our humanity, bend the knee, or just kill ourselves. <br /> <br /> Exalts begin to talk to each other. Organisations begin to talk to each other. Organisations talk to Exalts. Deep Seven, Anning Black, and Blue Hades is mentioned. Anning Black artifacts are picked up, and the twilights begin to look upon it. Lore-specced exalts look into the ruins, retrieving entire libraries worth of information from the rubble, while anyone with fighting skills worth having fight off the shoggoths that lurk within. Eclipses and other talkers enter and speak with Deep Seven and Blue Hades for a peace treaty. And a peace treaty that's worth the paper it's on, all the while they're trying to create spells to protect the walls of reality. A treaty is reached, taking in Blue Hades and Deep Seven resources in exchange for promises of protection. <br /> <br /> All this while, the walls of reality turn thinner and thinner. Until monsters are popping up left and right, and even the efforts of 700 celestial exalted are not enough to stem the tide. <br /> <br /> There are several things that make humanity susceptible to lovecraftian horrors. 1. They're vulnerability to possession, their nervous systems hijacked by entities. 2. Casting magic causes brain damage, meaning any mortal sorcerer is casting from hit points for anything more than cantrips. 3. Humans are not meant to cast magic, their very brains and minds unsuited for the coding that magic uses. 4. Humans live such terribly short lives. 5. Human technology is nothing compared to ANNING BLACK, BLUE HADES, or DEEP SEVEN.<br /> <br /> Obviously, this has to change. By this time, the masquerade is now and truly gone, the appearance and rampage of Bill Cipher like beings long since posted on the internet. The remaining governments of mankind (those that haven't fallen to gibbering horrors yet) marshall their forces together, working together as one under the Exalted, eclipes and other social manipulators acting as emissaries and diplomats to smooth over interactions. Twilights, alchemicals, and anyone that decided to pick lore as a favoured ability, start pumping out sorcerers and fighters, Legendary Scholar Curriculum pushing the limits of human intelligence and ability. Sorcerers begin working together, pushing the boundaries of what humans can do. Humans are weak. Humans are fragile. This weakness must be shed, without becoming an abomination. <br /> <br /> The increase in sorcerers is a godsend in smashing apart monsters from beyon space and time, but it further weakens the skeins of reality, being a short stopgap at best. And as the walls close in, a breakthrough is made. Natively, all exalts are stable and resistant to shaping effects. It was something built into them, due to the fact that they were meant to fight against beings who decreed things like 'up is down' and 'time shall move forward'. And thus, they hatched a plan. Making humans supremely powerful compared to what they were previously was an idea, but it would do nothing as the walls fall apart. It would be like if there was an MMA fighter, and the ground he was standing on fell apart. Humanity was strong, but to leverage that strength, they needed a stable base, something to stem the tide, and a safe haven. <br /> <br /> Thus project SAFE HARBOUR was born, stemming from the understanding of the stability of the Exaltations. The machines themselves would require an exalt to sit within, in stasis, meditating on the stability of reality, while the machines would amplify their stability and buttress the barriers between worlds. The machines are not all that powerful, and even with the help of the exalted, they can't cover everyone. <br /> <br /> The world's greatests infrastructure project began, grand arcologies and great Hive Cities being built. By this time, the human population had been decreased by 2/3rds, and was pretty much hanging on by the brink. Sidereals cast blessings upon the workers letting them move better than possible, while bureaucrats let the work go on despite the horrid conditions. In the end, sorcerous workings were placed on the arcologies, enchantments of longevity, fertility, health, and good luck placed on the cities to last them till the end of time. BLUE HADES, DEEP SEVEN, and humanity, all enter these places. <br /> <br /> And then the vaults closed, and none too late. As like a dam bursting, abominations burst from the walls, and the moon itself shattered, raining down on the ground like some accursed rain. This would normally be an apocalyptic occurrence, but considering everything that's occurred, this is actually pretty normal. Monsters run over what land remains, and horrors lurk in the abandoned cities as they slowly rot away. Wards and defences, maintained by exalt, thaumaturge, and servitor spirits, guard the entrances to the vaults.<br /> <br /> The siege begins. <br /> <br /> The defenders were empowered by fanaticism and fury, aided by wards and talismans and blessings, backed by thousands of programming cycles of computers and genetically engineered to the peak of humanity. The attackers were fearless automatons, slavering monsters, or simply beings that hungered for human souls. The clash between the two rang throughout space and time, bringing more and more abominations as they crawl from the dark points in reality searching for a meal. <br /> <br /> This battle lasted for centuries, in a stalemate. Exalts died, buying time for their companions to escape, in desperate final stands, or simply via dirty tricks. The pall of death hung over the heads of all who fought and lived within the fortress cities, where the sun shone a sick colour beyond description and the cries of horrors beyond imagination filled the air. Humanity would have killed themselves long ago, if it wasn't for Exalted using propaganda, music, and all the other forms of art to prevent the madness from grinding their minds to powder. <br /> <br /> Centuries passed, and eventually, the walls began to thicken as Earth moved into a different portion of space time. And as the walls of reality turned thicker, the tides turned. The attackers find it harder to enter reality, and the sounds of the dinner bell meant that less and less were coming here seeking the souls of the living. And slowly, ever so slowly, the tide of monsters became a trickle, and they began to push back, slowly crushing them one by one. Until, at last, the last one was dead. <br /> <br /> Humanity looked upon a world in ruin, where cities were long gone and the moon was shattered. But they were alive, and that was what mattered. The exalted exited their machines, and both they and humanity began to rebuild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T01:36:36-07:00","id":1344857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344781#post1344781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if someone's nice to his chosen in-group <i>most </i>of the time (except when he gets mad, then all bets are off), but outside that group he actively promotes genocide against another people, is he a nice guy?</div> </div> </div> </div>He did say 99%, not 100%. In Joshua, it's all &quot;God wanted us to wipe out every Canaanite, Amelikite and Blah-di-blah-ite, so we totally did&quot; and then in Judges, Kings, etc, those supposedly dead races are notably still there living just down the road from the Israelites and intermarrying with them and no-one seems bothered or shocked.<br /> <br /> But anyhow. Exalted, unlike say Dragon-Age, is supposed to be a non-Judeo-Christian fantasy (Fajad notwithstanding), with its demons taking influence more from Asian mythology (Yama Kings, Rakshasa, Oni, Yokai), and its Gods having that plus Roman (hence the Incarnae literally having the names of Roman gods) so I prefer not to think of Theion as Jehovah, but rather more like Plato's divine but uncaring architect, or the proto-Indo-European Deuz: the sky-god.<br /> <br /> Plus, Theion wasn't even the original leader of the Primordials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T01:36:56-07:00","id":1344858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344768#post1344768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of this theme is a deconstruction though; the Dragonblood's right to rule is based on a karmic system that (probably?) isn't true, the Solar are the rightful returning Kings, but why are they really rightful? (It's a bit Taergaryan-esque; they were usurped as the rightful rulers... except why were they rightful?) They usurped the previous rulers after all. In fact, is divine right (and Solars do, arguably, have Divine Right, being chosen by the Gods) really that rightful when the Gods themselves are imperfect?<br /> <br /> I mean, this is not to say that it's not an important theme of Exalted; it absolutely is! What makes legitimacy, who has legitimacy to rule, is a very key theme. But the theme isn't really exactly &quot;whose Divine Right is correct&quot;, that's just what the Solars and Dragonblood<i> think</i> is the theme of the story they're in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think you could use Exalted in the modern world as a look at religious legitimacy; messiahs and prophets with miraculous powers. Is this Solar the second coming of Jesus, the Antichrist, a Saint, or just a conmen using some kind of weird unknown tech to trick you into joining their cult?<br /> <br /> But you're basically introducing superheroes, and there's a reason that superhero stories generally don't revolve around the superheroes becoming the ruling <i>political</i> class (sometimes they do! But not generally). In our society, our idea of legitimacy is who best embodies the will of the people (expressed via voting), which doesn't really segue into super-skill. (Super-bureaucracy can help you maintain power via competence, but doesn't generally help you win power, as every candidate claims to be better at administration than the current guy. Super-presence and super-socialise is obviously very useful though, showing you can control your party.)<br /> <br /> If Britain suddenly got a Solar, I don't think anyone would argue that he/she should replace Elizabeth as our Queen. Nor that they should become Prime Minister, unless they get behind a programme of popular policies.<br /> (Obviously you can look into themes of what happens with a politician who can make people believe whatever they say, of course.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Your analysis mainly joins mine.<br /> <br /> I'm not advocating that &quot;Divine makes right&quot;, but as we both see it, it's a main theme for Exalted. My question, for importing Exalted characters in our contemporary world, is how would it work out ? Most western countries do not recognize any divine right to rule or be in charge, except for particular examples like for the example the Pope, and even in these cases he is elected by his peers through human consensus. I'd be interested to see how we would handle people having some sort of clear divine disposition, and what that means to our political choices.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T01:40:06-07:00","id":1344859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344790#post1344790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" c