re as a favoured ability, start pumping out sorcerers and fighters, Legendary Scholar Curriculum pushing the limits of human intelligence and ability. Sorcerers begin working together, pushing the boundaries of what humans can do. Humans are weak. Humans are fragile. This weakness must be shed, without becoming an abomination. <br /> <br /> The increase in sorcerers is a godsend in smashing apart monsters from beyon space and time, but it further weakens the skeins of reality, being a short stopgap at best. And as the walls close in, a breakthrough is made. Natively, all exalts are stable and resistant to shaping effects. It was something built into them, due to the fact that they were meant to fight against beings who decreed things like 'up is down' and 'time shall move forward'. And thus, they hatched a plan. Making humans supremely powerful compared to what they were previously was an idea, but it would do nothing as the walls fall apart. It would be like if there was an MMA fighter, and the ground he was standing on fell apart. Humanity was strong, but to leverage that strength, they needed a stable base, something to stem the tide, and a safe haven. <br /> <br /> Thus project SAFE HARBOUR was born, stemming from the understanding of the stability of the Exaltations. The machines themselves would require an exalt to sit within, in stasis, meditating on the stability of reality, while the machines would amplify their stability and buttress the barriers between worlds. The machines are not all that powerful, and even with the help of the exalted, they can't cover everyone. <br /> <br /> The world's greatests infrastructure project began, grand arcologies and great Hive Cities being built. By this time, the human population had been decreased by 2/3rds, and was pretty much hanging on by the brink. Sidereals cast blessings upon the workers letting them move better than possible, while bureaucrats let the work go on despite the horrid conditions. In the end, sorcerous workings were placed on the arcologies, enchantments of longevity, fertility, health, and good luck placed on the cities to last them till the end of time. BLUE HADES, DEEP SEVEN, and humanity, all enter these places. <br /> <br /> And then the vaults closed, and none too late. As like a dam bursting, abominations burst from the walls, and the moon itself shattered, raining down on the ground like some accursed rain. This would normally be an apocalyptic occurrence, but considering everything that's occurred, this is actually pretty normal. Monsters run over what land remains, and horrors lurk in the abandoned cities as they slowly rot away. Wards and defences, maintained by exalt, thaumaturge, and servitor spirits, guard the entrances to the vaults.<br /> <br /> The siege begins. <br /> <br /> The defenders were empowered by fanaticism and fury, aided by wards and talismans and blessings, backed by thousands of programming cycles of computers and genetically engineered to the peak of humanity. The attackers were fearless automatons, slavering monsters, or simply beings that hungered for human souls. The clash between the two rang throughout space and time, bringing more and more abominations as they crawl from the dark points in reality searching for a meal. <br /> <br /> This battle lasted for centuries, in a stalemate. Exalts died, buying time for their companions to escape, in desperate final stands, or simply via dirty tricks. The pall of death hung over the heads of all who fought and lived within the fortress cities, where the sun shone a sick colour beyond description and the cries of horrors beyond imagination filled the air. Humanity would have killed themselves long ago, if it wasn't for Exalted using propaganda, music, and all the other forms of art to prevent the madness from grinding their minds to powder. <br /> <br /> Centuries passed, and eventually, the walls began to thicken as Earth moved into a different portion of space time. And as the walls of reality turned thicker, the tides turned. The attackers find it harder to enter reality, and the sounds of the dinner bell meant that less and less were coming here seeking the souls of the living. And slowly, ever so slowly, the tide of monsters became a trickle, and they began to push back, slowly crushing them one by one. Until, at last, the last one was dead. <br /> <br /> Humanity looked upon a world in ruin, where cities were long gone and the moon was shattered. But they were alive, and that was what mattered. The exalted exited their machines, and both they and humanity began to rebuild.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some interesting stuff there. I like the siege hives, that's a bit different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T01:45:35-07:00","id":1344860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344858#post1344858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your analysis mainly joins mine.<br /> <br /> I'm not advocating that &quot;Divine makes right&quot;, but as we both see it, it's a main theme for Exalted. My question, for importing Exalted characters in our contemporary world, is how would it work out ? Most western countries do not recognize any divine right to rule or be in charge, except for particular examples like for the example the Pope, and even in these cases he is elected by his peers through human consensus. I'd be interested to see how we would handle people having some sort of clear divine disposition, and what that means to our political choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>No no no. You misunderstand something. <br /> <br /> Divine doesn't make right. <br /> <br /> Might makes right. Its just that gods have access to superpowers and essence and longevity, so of course they would say divinity makes right. <br /> <br /> Exalted excellencies are enough to let people punch up high enough. Someone of average talent and had taken a 3 week course in whatever she wants can spend motes to match trained professionals in that field, whether its cooking, politics, singing, dancing, accounting, or warfare. <br /> <br /> And then they get to the charms. <br /> <br /> So-called 'divine' right is nothing more than a fig leaf given out so that people won't resent you hard enough to rebel. Constantly use your power to kick down, and the ones beneath you would eventually gang up and shank you to death. Kick them down and justify yourself using 'divine' right, and you'll get a few patsies willing to defend you, and enough of a societal justification for people to ignore your dickishness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T02:20:45-07:00","id":1344863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344859#post1344859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's some interesting stuff there. I like the siege hives, that's a bit different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. <br /> <br /> And another one. <br /> <br /> So Poland got invaded by Germany. <br /> <br /> So I had a thought. There was definitely Jewish resistance to the Nazis. And there was most definitely sympathy for the nazis. And there was the death camps. And nobody gave a shit. <br /> <br /> So here's the idea. Some time before the nazis got the americans involved, but some time after the death camps, a band of freedom fighters sabotaged a bunch of nazi soldiers that were hunting down fleeing jews/ undesirables. The people fled, and the local cell decided to serve as a distraction, maintaining that no one should be sent to the death camps if they could help it. They flee with enemy soldiers in hot pursuit. They try to flee... but with enemies so close, they'll just get caught. There's no way to break contact. Someone must keep them away. <br /> <br /> That someone, was the cell leader. In comes our protag. A jewish woman who went to university, she is well educated, well taught, and well trained, having gone hunting and trained extensively while in the resistance cell. An owner of a chain of businesses, her income was wrecked when people boycotted and torched her businesses, and her husband and two sons were killed in a riot. Furious and angry, she saw her neighbours disappear one by one, and decided to act. <br /> <br /> Fun fact of being a resistance fighter. Its shitty. You get no pay, you get no support, you get no supply line, and your enemies are trained, motivated, and have better weapons than you. The woman has a rusty machine gun, a few hundred bullets, and one pistol with a single bullet for herself. <br /> <br /> She runs out to the last one, and has pulled out a knife, when the Unconquered Sun, seeing this woman's courage and selflessness in the face of adversity, graced her with his power. Dawn Caste, War supernal. <br /> <br /> Suffice it to say those men are not going back to their families. <br /> <br /> The next few months are slow for the German government. And did I say slow? I mean very slow. Our lady here had favoured in war, lore, firearms, bureaucracy, occult, athletics, subterfuge, and various other things. Paperwork is constantly lost, and has to be replaced. The bureaucracy grinds itself into gridlock, red tape and bureaucratic finanglings causing their response to move at a snail's pace. And all the while, the rebels are fighting back. Entire offices of the Gestapo go dark. Entire fleets of tanks and planes go silent. A city burns, and the one gibbering survivors screams of how they came out of the sewers and that everyone was dying. Skilled men and women of the Third Reich disappear, or just get found in their beds with their throat slit. Fires, explosions, and broken machinery in the factories, mean that Germany's already unfortunate supply problems begin to get even worse. <br /> <br /> And then shit happens. All this while, our Dawn caste has been stalking the shadows, stabbing people to death and grabbing vital documentation. And now, things change. The rampage guts Germany's army, shattering their core. Sent reeling, they pull back. At the same time, numerous guerilla fighters burst from what can be described as nowhere, leaping out of a sudden. Previous stormtroopers and soldiers find themselves with their pants down against supremely trained tiger warriors that have been trained via custom war charms to fight on the level of first circle demons. They find themselves torn to pieces, demolished, every ambush predicted and ever desperate attempt to counterattack effortlessly parried, once proud formations decimated by rebels who should by all means be cut down like scythe before a wheat. <br /> <br /> Britain pushes back, and old armies who either fled or deserted or in hiding join up with the main front, appearing suddenly and marching onto Berlin. The armies of the Third Reich pull back, wishing to protect their capital and their Fuhrer, while supply lines are cut off and the German lines in Russia find themselves overrun. <br /> <br /> The germans fight like demons, but they are faced down by Tiger Warriors led by a War supernal, who has a hand-held mortar and Accuracy Without Distance combined with Arrow Storm technique. In the end, the capital is broken to pieces, its defenses torn apart. <br /> <br /> Then the dawn caste strides into the bunker, and beheads half the nazi elite. The other half, is taken prisoner. Anyone who resists, and anyone with a gun in their hands and not part of the liberation army? Shot. <br /> <br /> Here's where things get hairy. Remember all the propaganda, of all the suberversives were out to destroy nazi germany, and so they had to be put down? Remember how majority of people in germany agreed with nazism, knew of the holocaust, and held auctions for people who had been sent to the gas chamber? Remember how people were perfectly willing to look the other way and ignore the death camps, or even send them back to Europe even when it was a death sentence? <br /> <br /> Remember how our dear dawn caste is someone who mass trained infiltrators to destroy and sabotage factories and vital infrastructure? Remember how our dawn caste mass trained a guerilla army to wipe out the Nazi Core? Remember how our dear dawn caste crushed an entire city which was devoted to the nazi war machine, killing them to the last man, woman, and child? Remember how she managed to pull a Creed, and pull an entire army out of seemingly nowhere? <br /> <br /> Think of it from the perspective of the Nazis. And I don't just mean the jackbooted thugs. I mean the civilians. <br /> <br /> Our Dawn Caste has won the war, stopping the holocaust before it could truly begin, putting in tens of thousands of documents on the heinous shit the nazis have done. But the appearance of a dawn caste who has shattered the nazi third reich may change the way history look upon eugenics and nazism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T02:26:08-07:00","id":1344864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344857#post1344857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He did say 99%, not 100%. In Joshua, it's all &amp;quot;God wanted us to wipe out every Canaanite, Amelikite and Blah-di-blah-ite, so we totally did&amp;quot; and then in Judges, Kings, etc, those supposedly dead races are notably still there living just down the road from the Israelites.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don\u2019t have to kill 100% of a people, down to the last individual, to commit genocide. The Nazis definitely committed genocide. but there are still Jewish people all over the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T02:28:57-07:00","id":1344865,"title":"","content":"Wait a minute. I'm saying that Jehovah was like pretty frickin' brutal. You know, what with the 'kill them all and tear out the bellies of pregant women' and 'kill them all down to the last animal' and 'kill them all and take the land for yourself cause I gave it to you'. <br /> <br /> I mean, am I the only guy who's finding a pattern here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T02:43:47-07:00","id":1344867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344860#post1344860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No no no. You misunderstand something.<br /> <br /> Divine doesn't make right.<br /> <br /> Might makes right. Its just that gods have access to superpowers and essence and longevity, so of course they would say divinity makes right.<br /> <br /> Exalted excellencies are enough to let people punch up high enough. Someone of average talent and had taken a 3 week course in whatever she wants can spend motes to match trained professionals in that field, whether its cooking, politics, singing, dancing, accounting, or warfare.<br /> <br /> And then they get to the charms.<br /> <br /> So-called 'divine' right is nothing more than a fig leaf given out so that people won't resent you hard enough to rebel. Constantly use your power to kick down, and the ones beneath you would eventually gang up and shank you to death. Kick them down and justify yourself using 'divine' right, and you'll get a few patsies willing to defend you, and enough of a societal justification for people to ignore your dickishness.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's your interpretation and I respect that, but you should try to think about human history and our relation to religion, and the relation of many things in Exalted to legitimacy. In Exalted, gods are gods of something, what makes it so ? What does it mean ? Would it make sense for a god of war to take the place of a god of disease ? Why ? Is it solely because of their dots in abilities or the size of their cult ?<br /> <br /> I'm not contesting makes make right to a certain extent in Exalted, but I think your analysis won't go far if you do not question it at all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T02:51:18-07:00","id":1344868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344867#post1344867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's your interpretation and I respect that, but you should try to think about human history and our relation to religion, and the relation of many things in Exalted to legitimacy. In Exalted, gods are gods of something, what makes it so ? What does it mean ? Would it make sense for a god of war to take the place of a god of disease ? Why ? Is it solely because of their dots in abilities or the size of their cult ?<br /> <br /> I'm not contesting makes make right to a certain extent in Exalted, but I think your analysis won't go far if you do not question it at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods? <br /> <br /> Because they are programs. They are servitors. They were built to be slaves. What makes a god of war the god of war? What's prevents him from taking the place of the god of disease? Because of metaphysics. I mean, he can apply for a change in job lots, but that greatly depends on the god of disease's own decisions. Maybe a sweet bribe will convince him to swap places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T03:01:36-07:00","id":1344869,"title":"","content":"How could the Unconquered Sun rebelled against his creators if he was just a program and a servitor ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T03:03:29-07:00","id":1344870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344864#post1344864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don\u2019t have to kill 100% of a people, down to the last individual, to commit genocide. The Nazis definitely committed genocide. but there are still Jewish people all over the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Jews killed 99% of the Canaanites, but left 1%, so that's okay&quot; is not what I was saying at all. I wasn't even saying &quot;The Jews killed 99% of the Canaanites.&quot;<br /> <br /> But... sigh, let's just leave it and get back to Exalted. Talk about Classical Roman mythology or ancient Chinese mythology, which are the main influences on Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-31-2019, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T03:05:41-07:00","id":1344871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344868#post1344868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gods?<br /> <br /> Because they are programs. They are servitors. They were built to be slaves. What makes a god of war the god of war? What's prevents him from taking the place of the god of disease? Because of metaphysics. I mean, he can apply for a change in job lots, but that greatly depends on the god of disease's own decisions. Maybe a sweet bribe will convince him to swap places.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this isn't quite consistent; being a program implies no choice, whereas you mention he can apply for a change, so Gods have some kind of free will, even if they're more fixed to their own nature than humans. (Well, humans are fixed to their own nature too, it's just less one that implies particular jobs.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T03:07:24-07:00","id":1344872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344870#post1344870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The Jews killed 99% of the Canaanites, but left 1%, so that's okay&quot; is not what I was saying at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t say you said it was <i>okay</i> - I\u2019m saying that if we\u2019re to take the Bible at its word, then the God therein directed people to commit genocide.*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344870#post1344870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... sigh, let's just leave it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> _________________________<br /> *And was unable to defeat an enemy tribe because their chariots were too badass for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T03:10:23-07:00","id":1344873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344867#post1344867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you should try to think about human history and our relation to religion, and the relation of many things in Exalted to legitimacy. In Exalted, gods are gods of something, what makes it so ? What does it mean ? Would it make sense for a god of war to take the place of a god of disease ? Why ? Is it solely because of their dots in abilities or the size of their cult ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... other than maybe the Unconquered Sun (as supreme King of Heaven), I don't think there's really a link between political legitimacy and what Gods are God of.<br /> Or, to put it another way, I don't see a link between the fact that Gods are constrained into certain natures and arguments for Solar (or Dragonblood, or Lunar) legitimacy.<br /> Unless you're just presenting different unrelated questions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T03:18:57-07:00","id":1344877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344873#post1344873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm... other than maybe the Unconquered Sun (as supreme King of Heaven), I don't think there's really a link between political legitimacy and what Gods are God of.<br /> Or, to put it another way, I don't see a link between the fact that Gods are constrained into certain natures and arguments for Solar (or Dragonblood, or Lunar) legitimacy.<br /> Unless you're just presenting different unrelated questions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is the god of something legitimate to take care of something is one of the questions I think could be interesting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T03:19:06-07:00","id":1344878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344871#post1344871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this isn't quite consistent; being a program implies no choice, whereas you mention he can apply for a change, so Gods have some kind of free will, even if they're more fixed to their own nature than humans. (Well, humans are fixed to their own nature too, it's just less one that implies particular jobs.)</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant, was, well, that gods were made for a purpose, and made with themselves specialised for jobs. That is to say, they were created for management. A new concept or discrete 'thing' pops up? A god appears, in the computer that is Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T03:33:01-07:00","id":1344883,"title":"","content":"So a being created atrificially is taking care of a whole aspect of Creation because an unexplainable and unspeakable force that would be &quot;the logic behind Creation&quot; decided so ? I'm fine with it but you are just making a rip-off of Demon : The Descent.<br /> <br /> Note that the final point is to try to include Exalted character in a modern settings, I'm coming up with these questions because we don't have an objective exhaustive book about our world that states why things were created and to what purpose. What is the place of the Exalted in such a setting, them who were chosen to fight against an established cosmological order ? What do the power of changing the purpose of existence means where there is no innate purpose of existence ? What makes them right to do it, then ? I know you are gonna say &quot;they can because they have the power to do so&quot;, but following this logic I could grab a knife and start stabbing people, would that be right ? I don't think so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T03:43:14-07:00","id":1344885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344883#post1344883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a being created atrificially is taking care of a whole aspect of Creation because an unexplainable and unspeakable force that would be &quot;the logic behind Creation&quot; decided so ? I'm fine with it but you are just making a rip-off of Demon : The Descent.<br /> <br /> Note that the final point is to try to include Exalted character in a modern settings, I'm coming up with these questions because we don't have an objective exhaustive book about our world that states why things were created and to what purpose. What is the place of the Exalted in such a setting, them who were chosen to fight against an established cosmological order ? What do the power of changing the purpose of existence means where there is no innate purpose of existence ? What makes them right to do it, then ? I know you are gonna say &quot;they can because they have the power to do so&quot;, but following this logic I could grab a knife and start stabbing people, would that be right ? I don't think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't this basically having the exaltations fall through a hole in space time, onto modern earth? <br /> <br /> I mean, forgive me, but this is inane. There was no 'right' or 'wrong'. There is no creator god for our reality, and even if there was one, I wouldn't give a damn. We had no purpose, no creator, and no grand plan for ourselves. Just self-replicating bags of carbon and water that manage to figure out the inanity and ridiculousness of existence before we wink out. <br /> <br /> Forever. <br /> <br /> The Exalted were meant to fight that which cannot be fought and come out victorious. And then they exceeded their limit, because Autochthon is an idiot. That moment in spy kids when the scientist said 'Do you think god, is there in heaven, because he too fears what he has created?'. That's what the Unconquered Sun felt.<br /> <br /> What are the Exalted for? They aren't sure yet, but they're sure as hell going to find out. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T03:52:22-07:00","id":1344886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344877#post1344877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is the god of something legitimate to take care of something is one of the questions I think could be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, now that is an interesting question! Certainly, while Gods tend to be skilled at their jobs, many are lazy, corrupt, foolish, distracted by politics, etc. It's certainly a theme/issue/story that's come up fairly often in games I play/run.<br /> <br /> Probably not one that comes up in &quot;Exalts go to the modern world&quot; (other, of course, than the Exalts themselves!) but it does come up with lots of settings with super-powered people who are in charge of things because... they're super-powered. 40K for example, is it right that a planet is ruled by Space Marines? (Space Marine-run planets tend to be pretty awful, as their main purpose is to produce warriors; the Space Marines don't care if people are miserable and starving if it makes them fight).<br /> <br /> Or in, say, a setting run by sorcerers who inherit their power by blood (which, arguably, is the issue in Exalted too!). Or a cyberpunk setting where the rich get genetically engineering and cybernetics to maintain their wealth.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T04:16:37-07:00","id":1344889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344885#post1344885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't this basically having the exaltations fall through a hole in space time, onto modern earth?<br /> <br /> I mean, forgive me, but this is inane. There was no 'right' or 'wrong'. There is no creator god for our reality, and even if there was one, I wouldn't give a damn. We had no purpose, no creator, and no grand plan for ourselves. Just self-replicating bags of carbon and water that manage to figure out the inanity and ridiculousness of existence before we wink out.<br /> <br /> Forever.<br /> <br /> The Exalted were meant to fight that which cannot be fought and come out victorious. And then they exceeded their limit, because Autochthon is an idiot. That moment in spy kids when the scientist said 'Do you think god, is there in heaven, because he too fears what he has created?'. That's what the Unconquered Sun felt.<br /> <br /> What are the Exalted for? They aren't sure yet, but they're sure as hell going to find out.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with your approach, but then what makes your approach of Exalted in our setting different than any power fantasy where some super powered guy grab the power ? You can brand it &quot;Exalted&quot; because you believe its their name, but Exalted is not just a name you put on someone with superpowers, it's about the themes of Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah, now that is an interesting question! Certainly, while Gods tend to be skilled at their jobs, many are lazy, corrupt, foolish, distracted by politics, etc. It's certainly a theme/issue/story that's come up fairly often in games I play/run.<br /> <br /> Probably not one that comes up in &quot;Exalts go to the modern world&quot; (other, of course, than the Exalts themselves!) but it does come up with lots of settings with super-powered people who are in charge of things because... they're super-powered. 40K for example, is it right that a planet is ruled by Space Marines? (Space Marine-run planets tend to be pretty awful, as their main purpose is to produce warriors; the Space Marines don't care if people are miserable and starving if it makes them fight).<br /> <br /> Or in, say, a setting run by sorcerers who inherit their power by blood (which, arguably, is the issue in Exalted too!). Or a cyberpunk setting where the rich get genetically engineering and cybernetics to maintain their wealth. </div> </div> </div>I'd argue Exigents exist, and they are chosen of gods of a particular subject, gods themselves whose purpose is to fulfill their duty. What does it make the Exigent in our world then ? I haven't read enough about them yet (and maybe there is just not enough writing about them at the time I'm writing this), but I believe one of the theme of Exigents can be : Must you fulfill the duty for which your god has sacrificied itself ? What sense does it make in Creation ? What sense does it make in our world ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T04:51:39-07:00","id":1344896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344889#post1344889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm fine with your approach, but then what makes your approach of Exalted in our setting different than any power fantasy where some super powered guy grab the power ? You can brand it &quot;Exalted&quot; because you believe its their name, but Exalted is not just a name you put on someone with superpowers, it's about the themes of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple. <br /> <br /> The Exalted ARE BETTER THAN YOU. <br /> <br /> That's the keyword. <br /> <br /> BETTER THAN YOU. <br /> <br /> Let's take an example. Strongman can lift several tons, can bench press a truck, and is basically near invincible. You want to hurt him? Get some artillery. <br /> <br /> What happens if strongman wants to become a leader? Well, he can punch up people. He can threaten them. <br /> <br /> But what usually happens is that he's no good at bureaucracy, management, leadership, politics, or swaying the crowd, and basically only has his personal power to fall back on. His fief becomes a brutal dictatorship, showing that might does not make right.<br /> <br /> Lets put it for more. Maybe he can throw fireballs. Maybe he's supers mart. Maybe he's got mind control. Maybe he's got supermoney powers. Maybe he's got super charisma.<br /> <br /> In those stories, you can just say &quot;But ah! He's a dictator!&quot; or you can say &quot;just because you've got superpowers doesn't mean that you'll be a good ruler!&quot; or 'he wasn't voted in! Thats illegitimate!&quot;. Either way, there's always something to show them to be wrong. <br /> <br /> What if you throw in an exalt? An exalt is basically potential, creating charms and new powers depending on what situation they find themselves in. <br /> <br /> An exalt takes power? How? Because an exalt with the barest dot in an ability can match a mortal who's trained for years to reach that level of skill. And that's them barely trying.<br /> <br /> So let's say that a solar exalt steps to the fray, and says &quot;let me be the ruler. For I am the greatest ruler to be.&quot; and he does it. Not just by punching up enemies. Charms purge corruption and inefficiency. Bureaucratic magic means that your stuff now takes a tenth of the time to process. The economy grows and grows and grows. Crime is at an all down low. Standards of living have never been better. All thanks to your solar god king. Same for a drsgonblooded. Or lunar. Or infernal. If the exalt so decides, he can rule better than nine tenths of the human race, and if he's willing to put in effort, surpass human ability all together.<br /> <br /> What happens when men are not equal? <br /> <br /> You want themes, @Chausse?<br /> <br /> Then riddle me this. In this world, we have gone through centuries of pain and misery to say that no one is inherently greater than other. Some may be better trained. Some may have better nutrition. And some may have the blessing of the gene dice. But nothing insurmountable, and in the end, all humans are roughly the same, barring a few exceptions that in the grand scheme of things don't quite matter. You see this theme all the time. Joe schmoe uses grit, hard work, and determination to beat someone who was &quot;supposedly&quot; his better.<br /> <br /> Well, the theme of Exalted is that that's bullshit. The weakest exalted can murder first circle demons by the dozens. Grab the world's 5 greatest mortals and throw them at a blood ape. And at least one of them will end up dead and a few others maimed permanently. Joe schmoe isn't going to beat an exalt that's decided to put effort in any kind of field of expertise. Athletics? Management? Mathematics? The exalt that actually tries and puts in effort will beat the mortal, hands down. Consistently. Always. <br /> <br /> All men are equal? If you were to say that in creation, you would be laughed out of town. And in a world where exaltation exists? Well, attitudes might change. When a single man can wreck an army on his own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T05:16:11-07:00","id":1344899,"title":"","content":"If they are so good, why were the Solar put down ? If the Dragon-blooded are so good, why is the Realm on the verge on a Civil War that may threaten the post powerful civilization in Creation ?<br /> <br /> There is one interesting question in your post that is &quot;What happens when men are not equal ?&quot;. Expand on it. Find ideas about it. Find unanswerable questions about it, and then try to answer them anyway.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, all men are equal is not a biological or genetic or whatnot expression in our western societies. They are constitutional rights, they are a societal agreement that all must subdue to the law of man before any other law. Why wouldn't the Exalted not be equal to anyone else ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T05:16:22-07:00","id":1344900,"title":"","content":"Accelerator, I don\u2019t think it\u2019s as simple or cut-and-dried as you\u2019re making it out to be.<br /> <br /> (It seldom is.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T05:18:47-07:00","id":1344901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344889#post1344889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue Exigents exist, and they are chosen of gods of a particular subject, gods themselves whose purpose is to fulfill their duty. What does it make the Exigent in our world then ? I haven't read enough about them yet (and maybe there is just not enough writing about them at the time I'm writing this), but I believe one of the theme of Exigents can be : Must you fulfill the duty for which your god has sacrificied itself ? What sense does it make in Creation ? What sense does it make in our world ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... in a different setting that doesn't have a ton of gods, how would Exigents work? I'm not sure they really would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T05:20:51-07:00","id":1344902,"title":"","content":"Accelerator - Be careful not to let your stories become nothing more than the expression of your own bias. Chausse is suggesting you think more about the topics you want to put in your stories and that's not a bad idea. Answering basically &quot;NO, it actually IS that simple&quot; is missing the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T05:24:33-07:00","id":1344903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344901#post1344901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm... in a different setting that doesn't have a ton of gods, how would Exigents work? I'm not sure they really would.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know I must admit, hence my questioning <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I went pretty far from my original questions about legitimacy and I'm less in questions I'm comfortable about because they didn't seem to appeal to Accelerator, but ultimately what interests me most comes back fo my earlier question :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well I guess some core themes I would be interested in would be legitimacy : In Exalted lots of characters have legitimacy because they have might or inherit some kind of legicimacy from greater sort of divine powers. Usually on earth this isn't the case, and I guess it could be a starting point : What is our relation to person wielding divine power, and why would we lend them political power (as people do in Exalted) ? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T06:05:25-07:00","id":1344916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344769#post1344769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what about Exaltations in Lovecraftian cosmic horror?</div> </div> </div> </div>A long hard fight filled with madness and tragedy which ends with the Exalted victorious but practically indistinguishable from the monsters they usurped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T06:23:14-07:00","id":1344921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344896#post1344896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when men are not equal? </div> </div> </div> </div>I think you'd really enjoy Progenitor by Greg Stolze.<br /> <br /> I also think we have very different interpretations of which truths we find to be self-evident.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T06:43:26-07:00","id":1344927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344903#post1344903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know I must admit, hence my questioning <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I went pretty far from my original questions about legitimacy and I'm less in questions I'm comfortable about because they didn't seem to appeal to Accelerator, but ultimately what interests me most comes back fo my earlier question :<br /> <br /> Well I guess some core themes I would be interested in would be legitimacy : In Exalted lots of characters have legitimacy because they have might or inherit some kind of legicimacy from greater sort of divine powers. Usually on earth this isn't the case, and I guess it could be a starting point : What is our relation to person wielding divine power, and why would we lend them political power (as people do in Exalted) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, to go back to this, Solars get their power from the Unconquered Sun, king of the Gods in Exalted. Dragonblood are exalted by/from the Dragons, the five supreme buildings of the world's largest religion.<br /> <br /> These divine beings don't exist in other settings (well, maybe classical-era Earth; Sol Invictus, Ra, Apollo, etc for Solars, literally Venus/Mars/Mercury for Sidereals), so there's not an obvious link.<br /> If someone in my city suddenly was surrounded by a burning golden aura and said they'd received it from Sol Invictus, most people would go &quot;uh, who?&quot; and some would say &quot;Oh, the obscure Roman sun god. There's no such thing.&quot; The assumption would be that there was some other explanation, and the Solar is just wrong.<br /> <br /> They could, of course, claim to have gotten the power from somewhere else, claiming to be the second coming of Christ, the Mahdi, the reincarnation of Buddha (or some other Bodhissatva). But that's a difficult one, because you have to fit what people expect; if you claim to be the second coming of Jesus, and that people should make you leader of the world, then you're going to find that whichever Christians believe you're acting in an unChristlike way (say, you've got 10 girlfriends, or you're a selfish jerk, or you just don't agree with their theoligical beliefs) may declare you the Antichrist or some such.<br /> And more significantly, the numbers make it difficult. Many religions believe one person will return to save the world, I can't think of one that expects 800 (though yogis or saints might work; again, that makes it awkward if you're acting very unsaintlike).<br /> <br /> So I think Accelerator's suggestion of psychic powers, aliens, mutation, etc, is more likely to be most people's explanation. And that doesn't lead into political legitimacy; it may lead into them being considered dangerous.<br /> <br /> That's in our world, in other settings there may be different explanations. In the Laundry Files, for example, when mass numbers of people start gaining a new form of power, everyone thinks its superpowers like in comic books, but those in the know think it's a new form of innate sorcery, and I guess they'd do the same for Solars.<br /> 40K might consider it a form of psychic power, or maybe saints (and whether you get branded a dangerous rogue psyker or a holy saint probably depends on how much you conform to local beliefs and the Inquisition). A superhero setting (say, Abberant) would probably put you into that.<br /> <br /> Again, most of these don't lead to political legitimacy the way &quot;chosen by a higher power&quot; does, because random mutation doesn't imply you've been carefully selected for your morality, wisdom, skill, etc, the way Divine Right or the Mandate of Heaven does.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T07:23:54-07:00","id":1344931,"title":"","content":"Thing is I'm not sure on what basis we are talking. To me an Exalted is someone chosen by gods to weild their power in the face of enemity (like, in the context of Exalted). If we are just talking about people with superpowers in our setting, then it's not Exalted, it's a Comic book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 10-31-2019, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T07:27:05-07:00","id":1344932,"title":"","content":"Sure, but I mean in terms of legitimacy, the gods who gave the Exalted their powers are not ones who exist in most settings, so no-one's going to consider them legitimate because they got powers from the Unconquered Sun or Dragons or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T07:37:17-07:00","id":1344933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344932#post1344932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but I mean in terms of legitimacy, the gods who gave the Exalted their powers are not ones who exist in most settings, so no-one's going to consider them legitimate because they got powers from the Unconquered Sun or Dragons or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, there's probably more than a few settings where if someone started radiating awesome power and attributed his ability to cast out sickness from people's bodies as being given by a god they haven't heard of, their response is, &quot;Tell me more about this 'Unconquered Sun' god...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T07:47:47-07:00","id":1344938,"title":"","content":"That's true. Many settings have plenty of Gods, what's one more?<br /> <br /> Though it also gets back to what the Solars themselves know; a lot of non-Zeniths never get a message from the Unconquered Sun that it was him who gave them their powers. They may get told by others (a Zenith, the Cult of the Illuminated, etc), or guess (I have a sun aura, maybe I was chosen by the Sun God?), but they may not. This has been an occasional debate in some of our games.<br /> <br /> So, while this doesn't apply so much if the Solars of Creation cross over, if people in a different setting start Exalting, they themselves may well not know where their power comes from, and interpret it through their own understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T07:52:41-07:00","id":1344939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344781#post1344781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if someone's nice to his chosen in-group <i>most </i>of the time (except when he gets mad, then all bets are off), but outside that group he actively promotes genocide against another people, is he a nice guy?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're really interested in debating the issue, we can take it to Private Messages, but you're complaining about a story you haven't actually read.<br /> <br /> Exactly like one of those people who never actually read or watched Game of Thrones, and use rumors as the basis to complain that Danyerus was just a White Savior who always reveled in bloodshed without concern for the people she hurt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T08:29:33-07:00","id":1344950,"title":"","content":"I can't imagine telling an Exalted in the modern world (not our world, but an analogue) that wasn't already better told in Kingdom Come. (You could argue Watchmen, but then we'd have to knife fight).<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm fiddling with the idea of an Exalted in Chronicles of Darkness crossover that reads like something between Chrono Trigger (G-M as a Lavos analogue, obviously) and cosmic tier Unknown Armies. It's a silly-silly idea that mostly tugs at the heartstrings of my trench coats and katana sub-genre loving self, and it would be an absolute trainwreck, but I would pay serious change to run (or better yet play in) such a setting.<br /> <br /> As for the more thematic / meta elements, all this talk of how the Exalted would or wouldn't effect the setting (or our world) really comes down to a sociological perspective. Do you believe in the Great Man... eh, ideology? Do you take a wider assumption to societies? How far do you think supernatural aptitude could carry a person?<br /> <br /> Like, no three folks can agree on how society runs or what moral legitimacy means, but stortelling is an exercise in exploring these concepts and pinning down a narrative that at bare minimum gas stuff to say about these questions. Even if you disagree with the ST's views, the result can still be fascinating.<br /> <br /> Granted, that all comes out in the breakfast, not the sausage making process we're discussing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T08:59:31-07:00","id":1344956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344939#post1344939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you're complaining about a story you haven't actually read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you tell me what I have and haven't read.<br /> <br /> I <i>grew up</i> with stories of crosses and disciples and loaves and fishes and arks and serpents and locusts and commandments and parted seas. My grandparents took me to church-sponsored plays where screaming, begging sinners were thrown into the lake of fire. I attended Sunday schools and church camp and sang all the songs. I've taken communion and been baptized.<br /> <br /> Do you know what made me realize Christianity wasn't my cup of tea?<br /> <br /> \u200b<i>Actually reading from the Bible</i>, without having my hand held as I journeyed through it.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Also, meeting LGBT people who weren't the wicked monsters my pastors portrayed them as.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-31-2019, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T09:26:11-07:00","id":1344959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344956#post1344956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you tell me what I have and haven't read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> But are you willing to read it again? Not while having your hand held, but while having a companion to whom you can accuse the story and demand a defense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T09:36:17-07:00","id":1344961,"title":"","content":"Last time I tried that, it ended up with a guy shouting me down with &quot;The Jews killed Jesus!&quot; over and over. So, I'll pass on that for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T09:37:05-07:00","id":1344962,"title":"","content":"I'm actually interested in hearing interpretations about the Bible as well if it can allow me to have greater subtetly narrating histories of Exalted","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T09:46:28-07:00","id":1344965,"title":"","content":"Sorry to hear that Alucard. Your pastors sound like assholes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344950#post1344950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm fiddling with the idea of an Exalted in Chronicles of Darkness crossover that reads like something between Chrono Trigger (G-M as a Lavos analogue, obviously)</div> </div> </div> </div>G-M?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a silly-silly idea that mostly tugs at the heartstrings of my trench coats and katana sub-genre loving self, and it would be an absolute trainwreck, but I would pay serious change to run (or better yet play in) such a setting. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the Exalted in Chronicles of Darkness works much better for katana and trench coats than the normal Chronicles/World of Darkness which people try and run as katana+trenchcoats, when it's supposed to be a very serious horror setting.<br /> (I did once do a Sabbat game which was all about the katana and trenchcoats. PCs held their guns sideways, and once carried out a series of bloody breaking+enterings so as to acquire a full set of Die Hard DVDs. Sabbat works well for that.)<br /> Whereas Exalted are much more about action genre tropes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the more thematic / meta elements, all this talk of how the Exalted would or wouldn't effect the setting (or our world) really comes down to a sociological perspective. Do you believe in the Great Man... eh, ideology? Do you take a wider assumption to societies? How far do you think supernatural aptitude could carry a person? </div> </div> </div>To some extent this is a very good point, and was partly what I was saying earlier about the ability of a Solar to effect change in a grand sc-fi setting; can any one man/woman change the lives of a billion billion humans?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, of course, our so-called &quot;Great Men&quot; are just, well, humans. They may have been a bit smarter than average or something, but they weren't magical heroes. It may be fair to argue that Great Man theory isn't true in the real world, but would be for Exalts. In fact, that's kind of an assumption of the game, and one that distinguishes itself from other settings; your characters can, and are expected to, make big changes to the setting. Unlike, say, Shadowrun, which has a developing metaplot that your PCs are not generally assumed to drastically change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if you disagree with the ST's views, the result can still be fascinating. </div> </div> </div>This is definitely true, though it has led us into some big arguments about whether or not the PCs' plans ought to be successful!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T09:57:12-07:00","id":1344968,"title":"","content":"I'm not quite sure what the discussions on god is about. I mean, I presume that we're talking about the modern setting, where we don't have the Exalted rpg. Why would we even call it gods? Look at our current religions. Christianity, Buddhism, Taoism, Islam.... none of them really have any mythos or religious rules for when people start glowing a certain colour and carry out miraculous actions. And atheism is of no help. I mean, I made an atheist exalt, and she has literally no idea she is a Copper Spider, Twilight Caste, Chosen of the Unconquered Sun, inheritor of a legacy a thousand years in the making. <br /> <br /> And besides, let's be honest here. From what I can remember of my old Revelations sermons, before Christ returns to earth as the second coming, there is the anti-christ, who will basically take over the world. And I'm fairly sure the anti-christ is described as having supernatural powers. Which spells bad things for our Exalt if he believes in this. <br /> <br /> I mean, even if all is fine and dandy, they don't know of the Unconquered Sun, the primordial war, or the Usurpation. All the sun says to his zeniths are 'be great and righteous in my name'. I'm not even sure if he would actually tell him his name. Even less for the other castes. Sidereals just start glowing and have nothing told to them by the Maidens. Lunars get a visit from the Witch-goddess, but I'm not quite sure how much she talks, or that she'll talk in this new setting. All in all, for all intents and purposes, Exalted do not know they are Exalted. They may say 'magic' or 'aliens' or 'psychic powers' or 'the devil!'. But 'Chosen of the gods Sol Invictus, Luna, and the 5 Maidens' is pretty darned out there.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T10:02:46-07:00","id":1344970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344965#post1344965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">G-M?</div> </div> </div> </div>god machine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, the Exalted in Chronicles of Darkness works much better for katana and trench coats than the normal Chronicles/World of Darkness which people try and run as katana+trenchcoats, when it's supposed to be a very serious horror setting.<br /> (I did once do a Sabbat game which was all about the katana and trenchcoats. PCs held their guns sideways, and once carried out a series of bloody breaking+enterings so as to acquire a full set of Die Hard DVDs. Sabbat works well for that.)<br /> Whereas Exalted are much more about action genre tropes. </div> </div> </div>That's the hope! I think it comes down to enjoying the WoD aesthetic, but not so much the tales of horror in general. Enjoyable once in a while, but ultimately not my bag.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To some extent this is a very good point, and was partly what I was saying earlier about the ability of a Solar to effect change in a grand sc-fi setting; can any one man/woman change the lives of a billion billion humans? </div> </div> </div>Thanks! And yeah, was picking up on what you posted earlier. We just don't know enough about society and how behaviour works to say with certainty, but the game world can be an interesting way to explore the idea, assuming everyone is on the same page.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other hand, of course, our so-called &amp;quot;Great Men&amp;quot; are just, well, humans. They may have been a bit smarter than average or something, but they weren't magical heroes. It may be fair to argue that Great Man theory isn't true in the real world, but would be for Exalts. In fact, that's kind of an assumption of the game, and one that distinguishes itself from other settings; your characters can, and are expected to, make big changes to the setting. Unlike, say, Shadowrun, which has a developing metaplot that your PCs are not generally assumed to drastically change. </div> </div> </div> Definitely true that the &quot;great&quot; folks in Exalted are nothing like those we'd point to in the real world, but I'm not sure Exalted definitively supports G-man theory even within its setting. There's an awful lot about social pressures and assumptions in how the Dynasty operates, how The Bull of the North's rebellion or Panther's personal enlightenment that bends towards a more social perspective.<br /> <br /> But, all that is better hashed out as a theme explored in the game rather than something explicitly defined. Or it could never come up, like if one is going for a Katana and Trenchcoat vibe =D<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is definitely true, though it has led us into some big arguments about whether or not the PCs' plans ought to be successful! </div> </div> </div>I like to leave oughtta for dice and npc motivations / reactions to resolve, but it's hard to apply with any kind of (honest) objectivity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T10:06:18-07:00","id":1344971,"title":"","content":"I tend to interpret the Exalted books as being somewhat critical of the Great Man theory; the Exalted are just as much a product of the world that exists around them as any person in our world, after all.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/doom-and-gloam\" target=\"_blank\">\u200b(Except for magical librarians that <i>may</i> have been read into existence by raksha.)</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T10:10:26-07:00","id":1344972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344962#post1344962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually interested in hearing interpretations about the Bible as well if it can allow me to have greater subtetly narrating histories of Exalted</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's kind of an absolute ton. It's the world's most influential book (and of course, it's not even one book with one author, it's 66-72 books with authors seperated by hundreds or even a thousand years, and they're all different genres) after all, different cultures have interpreted it differently, and people within one culture interpret it differently. In Britain we've got about 7 or 8 significant Christian denominations, and a few different Jewish groups, but when I talked to Americans you guys seem to have about a million different kinds of Churches. (Though I imagine some have pretty similar interpretations).<br /> And that's not even getting into the historical interpretations, which I find quite interesting. And also looking at wider semitic myths (like all the Babylonian and Akkadian and Sumerian versions of the flood myth).<br /> <br /> For the purpose of Exalted, you probably mostly want to look at Judges and Kings anyway, rather than most of the Bible. I found rereading Judges in light of having read about the collapse of the Bronze Age and the invasions of Sea people very interesting, as there's little references to it (like mentioning how everyone's stopped using the roads). You could use that as an inspiration for a post-Contagion world. And Kings works well for general Southern swords-and-sandals games.<br /> <br /> I would say though, that while one of my friends is doing a Noah's Ark thing with his game, and I've used references to Enki a bit, generally for Exalted the influences are more Chinese and Graeco-Roman mythology. I guess Solars have a bit of an OT-Prophet thing going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-31-2019, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T10:26:56-07:00","id":1344975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344968#post1344968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would we even call it gods? Look at our current religions. Christianity, Buddhism, Taoism, Islam.... none of them really have any mythos or religious rules for when people start glowing a certain colour and carry out miraculous actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you could argue &quot;I'm a saint!&quot; or &quot;I'm a Yogi!&quot; If you're the only one, you might get away with it. But it'd be difficult to argue when there's several hundred others claiming to be the same in completely different religions. It's kind of difficult to argue your anima is your Angelic halo because you've been chosen by Jesus if down the street there's a guy with the exact same powers who claims it's because he's the reincarnation of a Boddhisattva, and another who claims he's just a wizard, and another who claims she's an alien psychic.<br /> <br /> So I think while in the early stages you might get religious interpretations, later I think you'll get more scientific (or pseudo-scientific) explanations.<br /> Now, when those also fail, you might get some kind of Exalt-worshipping cult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From what I can remember of my old Revelations sermons, before Christ returns to earth as the second coming, there is the anti-christ, who will basically take over the world. And I'm fairly sure the anti-christ is described as having supernatural powers. Which spells bad things for our Exalt if he believes in this. </div> </div> </div>That's Premillenial Dispensationalism. It's a common belief amongst American evangelicals, but not so common elsewhere (though it does exist). It's not the interpretation of the Catholic or Orthodox Church.<br /> Revelation talks about a giant dragon marauding around the world, and a beast that makes people worship it (the beast's number, 616, is a numerological reference to Emperor Nero, I wonder why that could be?), and all the Kings of the world coming together to fight God, and then Jesus returns. The word Antichrist is never used (there's a different book, 2 Peter IIRC, which says people who preach that Jesus only came to Earth in a spiritual way and not with a physical body, are Antichrists).<br /> <br /> So, anyway, my point is that people in, say, Italy, are probably not going to think a bad Solar is the Antichrist. But I guess maybe people in Texas might. (Though again, if there's 300 Solars, some good, some bad, that doesn't really fit with one supreme evil guy. But people are very good at stretching stuff.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, even if all is fine and dandy, they don't know of the Unconquered Sun, the primordial war, or the Usurpation. All the sun says to his zeniths are 'be great and righteous in my name'. I'm not even sure if he would actually tell him his name. Even less for the other castes. Sidereals just start glowing and have nothing told to them by the Maidens. Lunars get a visit from the Witch-goddess, but I'm not quite sure how much she talks, or that she'll talk in this new setting. All in all, for all intents and purposes, Exalted do not know they are Exalted. They may say 'magic' or 'aliens' or 'psychic powers' or 'the devil!'. But 'Chosen of the gods Sol Invictus, Luna, and the 5 Maidens' is pretty darned out there. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-31-2019, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T10:34:27-07:00","id":1344978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344971#post1344971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to interpret the Exalted books as being somewhat critical of the Great Man theory; the Exalted are just as much a product of the world that exists around them as any person in our world, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is and it isn't; it accepts the premise that one person can have a huge influence on the world, and that some people are much &quot;greater&quot; than others (in a skill and ability sense, not a moral sense, though some players/writers like to consider Solars the &quot;good guys&quot;). But it does like to explore and deconstruct a lot of the other parts, as you mention. The social pressures of Dynasts and how that makes them the product of a certain society, for example. (This came up last session I played actually, the extent to which Dynastic support for slavery is inevitable, being products of a pro-slavery society).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T10:40:20-07:00","id":1344982,"title":"","content":"Hence &quot;somewhat.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T10:41:15-07:00","id":1344984,"title":"","content":"But frankly speaking, what would be the reaction to people with actual superpowers? <br /> <br /> Because I&quot;m writing a story with the same premise 'Exalts in modern earth'. And for me? I think they'll react with fear. Mostly awe and happiness, because its so gosh darn amazing. But then fear, as the exalts get stronger and stronger. And realize that, yes, there are heroes now. They kill dragons. But they're the peasants who get their village burned down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T10:46:03-07:00","id":1344986,"title":"","content":"That sounds about right, tbh, especially when people can't explain <i>why</i> these people have these powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T10:49:50-07:00","id":1344987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344965#post1344965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to hear that Alucard. Your pastors sound like assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Pharisees who used outward displays of &quot;virtue&quot; to grab authority, and who distracted from their own sins by pointing to acceptable targets.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344961#post1344961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last time I tried that, it ended up with a guy shouting me down with &quot;The Jews killed Jesus!&quot; over and over. So, I'll pass on that for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was offering a Private Conversation, so no one could interrupt us by saying such a stupid thing.<br /> <br /> By which I mean, it's no more true than the fact that Christianity is a JEWISH movement, centered around a Jewish man who claimed to be the son of the Jewish god, and whose teachings were initially spread by Jews, and whose movement was exclusively led by Jews until the Roman Empire destroyed the Jewish nation by destroying their holy city and temple and scattering the Jewish people across the entire known world, thus causing their language and culture to nearly vanish from the Earth.<br /> <br /> The Catholics see &quot;Saint Peter&quot; as the first pope, and Peter was born Simon, a Jewish man.<br /> <br /> Those who want to hate the Jewish people don't actually care about God or Jesus. Such a person just wants to hurt people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T10:57:32-07:00","id":1344988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344986#post1344986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds about right, tbh, especially when people can't explain <i>why</i> these people have these powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <br /> <br /> Oh, sure, she seems like a total badass, except for the major healing powers due to a medicine supernal and several custom charms. But to an american audience that's seen John Wick? She's pretty normal. Sure, she's a little girl who can beat up dozens of grown soldiers, but hey, we've already seen the badass normal tropes and Black Widow. <br /> <br /> Things start to change when she starts using Essence 3 athletics charms. Like mountain crossing leap and racing hare method. It doesn't matter how much someone is called or insists on 'an ordinary person except that I have healing powers' when she can break the speed limit and leap over entire buildings in a single bound. Imagine that. Someone who can move at 50 miles per hour, and disappear in a burst of light and sound and reappear miles away. Someone who has taken resistance charms (to boost soak) and can ignore grenades exploding right next to her. <br /> <br /> <br /> They start asking inconvenient questions, like 'by what rhythm or reason does she gain her powers'. The answer is simple and easy for anyone to see. Barring medicine (she was a self-taught doctor when she exalted). All of her powers appear to come one after another, after training. She trains to use a computer? God-mind algorithms. She trains in arts and crafts? Crack-mending technique and impurity hammering blow and Craftsman needs no tools. She jogs and runs around? She gets racing hare method and mountain crossing leap.<br /> <br /> Which means that she can gain nearly any kind of conceivable power, as long as she decides to train for it and there's some way to logically extend her training to what she's doing. She can treat wounds, so she can have patients come back from injuries in a single day where it would normally take a decade. She's trained herself to ignore pain and become more durable, like martial arts training, so she can walk past explosions. And so on and so forth. <br /> <br /> Which means that she's a lot more dangerous than she should be, which means, well, bad shit for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T11:05:06-07:00","id":1344989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344988#post1344988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, she's a little girl who can beat up dozens of grown soldiers, but hey, we've already seen the badass normal tropes and Black Widow.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, cinematic badasses only get to look like badasses because their opponents will just patiently attack one at a time. A person <i>actually</i> dodging bullets and easily taking down a dozen trained soldiers with her fists is just as blatantly inhuman as the one using Mountain-Crossing Leap Technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-31-2019, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T11:19:05-07:00","id":1344994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344988#post1344988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.<br /> <br /> Oh, sure, she seems like a total badass, except for the major healing powers due to a medicine supernal and several custom charms. But to an american audience that's seen John Wick? She's pretty normal. Sure, she's a little girl who can beat up dozens of grown soldiers, but hey, we've already seen the badass normal tropes and Black Widow.</div> </div> </div> </div>People know John Wick is fiction though, they don't expect to see it in real life. They certainly don't expect it from a little girl.<br /> <br /> Still, the &quot;can train herself to be amazing at anything&quot; probably looks more like a prodigy than something supernatural at low Essence, and it's easy to hide from others, so I see your point about maybe it not looking too extraordinary until Essence 3 (especially because she probably doesn't need to actually do any fighting at the beginning, so may not give it away that way).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T11:24:17-07:00","id":1344998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1344994#post1344994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People know John Wick is fiction though, they don't expect to see it in real life. They certainly don't expect it from a little girl.<br /> <br /> Still, the &amp;quot;can train herself to be amazing at anything&amp;quot; probably looks more like a prodigy than something supernatural at low Essence, and it's easy to hide from others, so I see your point about maybe it not looking too extraordinary until Essence 3 (especially because she probably doesn't need to actually do any fighting at the beginning, so may not give it away that way).</div> </div> </div> </div>One story idea I had was her in a battle of wits against either a retired general, or a chess grandmaster.<br /> <br /> They've got nine dice. She's intelligence 4, with a few weeks to prepare. She's got war 1.<br /> <br /> She wins. <br /> <br /> I mean, I'm not sure what you mean? Its OK to say that theyre a prodigy but when the exalt can match professionals with a few weeks worth of effort, it starts getting scary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T11:31:46-07:00","id":1345000,"title":"","content":"I mean that they're going to go &quot;wow, that's amazing&quot; not &quot;there must be something supernatural here&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T11:34:26-07:00","id":1345001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345000#post1345000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean that they're going to go &quot;wow, that's amazing&quot; not &quot;there must be something supernatural here&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You and I have very different definitions of supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T11:41:00-07:00","id":1345005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345001#post1345001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You and I have very different definitions of supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't be the first time someone on these forums hinged their discussion on terms they defined differently without realizing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T11:42:11-07:00","id":1345006,"title":"","content":"Well... what do you guys define 'supernatural' as?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T11:49:42-07:00","id":1345009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345006#post1345006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... what do you guys define 'supernatural' as?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Attributed to some force beyond the understanding of science or the laws of nature.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bOne person beating another person at a game of wits is not supernatural. Nothing about that flies in the face of our understanding of the world around us. A human moving faster than a bullet <i>is supernatural</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T11:53:09-07:00","id":1345011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345009#post1345009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Attributed to some force beyond the understanding of science or the laws of nature.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bOne person beating another person at a game of wits is not supernatural. Nothing about that flies in the face of our understanding of the world around us. A human moving faster than a bullet <i>is supernatural</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my example above, a little girl that's got 1 dot (she's read sun tzu's art of war and a few online courses) can beat a general that graduated from West Point and had half a century's worth of experience and in understanding of battle strategy.<br /> <br /> That is beyond the laws of nature. At least, such a thing is so absurd that its crazy bullshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T11:59:16-07:00","id":1345014,"title":"","content":"You keep mentioning her size and her gender like it's a strike against her ability to do these things. It isn't.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, people can think strategically without having battlefield experience - that she's got such a high Intelligence suggests she probably does it all the time.<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200bThe fact is, generals <i>can</i> and <i>do</i> lose. It may be <i>improbable</i> for such a decorated individual to find himself so soundly beaten by an untested youth, but it is not <b>impossible</b>. (Especially when we've established that this girl is an accomplished intellectual.)<br /> <br /> \u200bThis is especially silly considering you're representing this with traits representing <b>rolled dice</b>. It's entirely possible for the general to roll no successes and at least one one, meaning he botches his roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-31-2019, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T12:06:57-07:00","id":1345017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345001#post1345001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You and I have very different definitions of supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually thinking more about people's resistance to believing in the supernatural. If there's a non-supernatural explanation (luck, cheating, prodigy, etc) that's what sceptics will go for.<br /> <br /> Like... my grandma told me that, after my granddad's death, he haunted her house for 6 months. Made the light she'd bought him come on and off, turned the TV on and off, that kind of thing. Once the fire alarm went off in the middle of the night, but she woke up and half-asleep said &quot;Geoff, shut up, I'm trying to sleep!&quot; and the fire alarm stopped by itself. After six months, she decided he must be scared he'd be forgotten, so she put a photo of him up in the hall, and all the electrical problems stopped.<br /> <br /> But... I don't believe her. Do I have an explanation for the weirdness? Honestly, not a very good one. I assume she imagined it all somehow, but my grandma is a very practical, down-to-earth, even pretty cynical woman. But... I don't believe in ghosts. So I assume there must be a different explanation, even if &quot;ghost granddad&quot; actually explains all the evidence better than anything I can think up. Because... I just don't believe in ghosts.<br /> <br /> Similarly, my nan was once on a train and spent 15 minutes talking to the woman in her carriage. She went to the loo, came back, and the woman was gone. She went and asked around, and everyone said she was the only one in the carriage, no woman of that name had bought a ticket, etc. My nan never had any mental health problems. She wasn't sure, but wondered if it was a ghost.<br /> Again, I don't have a good explanation, but I don't believe in ghosts, so I'm going to put this down to mistakes by everyone else. Because I just don't think ghosts are real.<br /> <br /> So I think unless it's really in your face blatant, most people will try to find an explanation of Solars that fits into their worldview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-31-2019, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T12:14:18-07:00","id":1345018,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> Like, your example was a character who normally has five dice, against an opponent with nine.<br /> <br /> \u200bLet's assume no stunts whatsoever, just straight up dice against dice. Fistful of d10s in my hand, and...<br /> <br /> \u200bFor the general, I got 1,2,4,4,5,<b>8</b>,4,1,2. One success.<br /> For your Twilight, I got <b>7</b>,<b>8</b>,3,<b>7</b>,2. Three successes.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>With no magic whatsoever</b>, she just beat him. She beat <i>his ass</i>.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I <i>am</i> a little surprised that it happened on my first try, though - I was expecting to have to do this two or three times before she managed to whup him up and down the street.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-31-2019, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T12:24:52-07:00","id":1345019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345011#post1345011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my example above, a little girl that's got 1 dot (she's read sun tzu's art of war and a few online courses) can beat a general that graduated from West Point and had half a century's worth of experience and in understanding of battle strategy.<br /> <br /> That is beyond the laws of nature. At least, such a thing is so absurd that its crazy bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>......No? No it is not? As history can tell you, great and glorious generals..... sometimes lose.<br /> <br /> Besides.....&quot;Beat&quot;.... at what? Tactics? That isn't the generals job, that is the responsibility of all of their underlings, down to the squad-level NCOs. Strategy? That is the culmination of the generals <i><b>dozens</b></i> of support-staff, from staff <i>specialized</i> in planning to those <i>specialized</i> in logistics. Logistics? Again, part of his job, but not really.<br /> <br /> You are so severely misconstruing how.... well, &quot;reality&quot; works it isn't even applicable to your question. Yet another example of why trying to compare Exalted to &quot;the real world&quot; <u><i>using Exalted mechanics</i></u> is a fools-errand at best.<br /> <br /> I also really want to know what troops this Twilight has. Even 10,000 Blood Apes versus 2,000 modern soldiers are going to see the Blood Apes reduced to stains on the floor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","user":"Boston123","date":". 10-31-2019, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T12:27:21-07:00","id":1345020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345019#post1345019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides.....&quot;Beat&quot;.... at what?</div> </div> </div> </div>He already said, &quot;a battle of wits.&quot; Implied it might be chess, but didn't say explicitly.<br /> <br /> Which, yeah. Not impossible for a general to lose at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T12:32:04-07:00","id":1345021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345019#post1345019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also really want to know what troops this Twilight has. Even 10,000 Blood Apes versus 2,000 modern soldiers are going to see the Blood Apes reduced to stains on the floor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Modern soldiers have guns that can hit dematerialised spirits and are better in hand-to-hand than super strong demons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T12:32:29-07:00","id":1345022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345020#post1345020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He already said, &amp;quot;a battle of wits.&amp;quot; Implied it might be chess, but didn't say explicitly.<br /> <br /> Which, yeah. Not impossible for a general to lose at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chess, battle simulations, checkers, or a war game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T12:34:03-07:00","id":1345024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345020#post1345020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He already said, &quot;a battle of wits.&quot; Implied it might be chess, but didn't say explicitly.<br /> <br /> Which, yeah. Not impossible for a general to lose at.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not even bringing up the idea(s) that:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Being &quot;good&quot; or &quot;bad&quot; at chess doesn't necessarily mean you are intelligent, or unintelligent</li> <li>Being &quot;good&quot; or &quot;bad&quot; at chess doesn't mean you can't be &quot;good&quot; at your actual job (aka, &quot;generaling&quot;)</li> <li>&quot;wits&quot; has no actual correlation between other skills. One can be &quot;witty&quot; (not even touching the question of &quot;what is 'wits'?&quot;), and be unable to lead their way out of a wet paper bag.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T12:40:04-07:00","id":1345027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345022#post1345022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chess, battle simulations, checkers, or a war game.</div> </div> </div> </div>A skilled person losing at any of these doesn't break any known laws of physics; in fact, if you pit <i>two </i>chess grandmasters against one another, it will not cause the universe to implode on itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345024#post1345024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even bringing up the idea(s) that:</div> </div> </div> </div>4. A person who's &quot;good&quot; at chess can still have an off-day, be sick or distracted or emotionally-compromised, not really bring their A-game, or even just plain <i>not want to win</i> this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-31-2019, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T12:47:03-07:00","id":1345028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345021#post1345021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Modern soldiers have guns that can hit dematerialised spirits and are better in hand-to-hand than super strong demons?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Blood Apes have to materialize in order to attack, no?<br /> <br /> Modern armies have squads made up of multiple soldiers, each with their own rapid-fire weapons. Even if only one member of the squad notices the apes materializing, they have <i><u>30</u></i> bullets, which are <i>much</i> more dangerous than spears and arrows, to shoot into the Blood Ape. Oh, and the soldiers can do this from any range, while the Blood Ape has only 1 ranged attack.<br /> <br /> My mortal players have killed Blood Apes in close-combat before, with the aforementioned spears, swords and arrows. It wasn't easy, but it was possible. Modern weapons would level the playing field even more. <br /> <br /> However, even if a Blood Ape is more than a match for a squad of soldiers..... the soldiers have grenades, heavy weapons, vehicles with their own heavy weapons, artillery and more, stuff that most of Creation <i>wishes</i> it had. And if there are 10,000 Blood Apes ravening for blood, the army is <i>going to use that stuff</i>.<br /> <br /> I suggest you read <i><a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Literature/TheSalvationWar\" target=\"_blank\">Salvation War</a> (</i>if you can find it online nowadays) for an idea of what happens when Demons (and Angels, for that matter), go up against a modern industrialized army (or, really, armies). Its.... not pretty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T12:54:09-07:00","id":1345029,"title":"","content":"Obviously, the best way to deal with this is to arm the blood apes. Give them body armour, giant shotguns, and top hats and pinstripe suits, and the playing field will be levelled.<br /> <br /> Edit: and oh yeah. The salvation war? Really? You're using that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T13:04:59-07:00","id":1345033,"title":"","content":"Read it. Not impressed.<br /> <br /> 2000 of the Blood Apes walk, Immaterial into Close range of the soldiers. The soldiers smell rotten meat and hear gnashing of teeth -- maybe a few of them fire bullets into the air. The Blood Apes literally walk through tank armor and into artillery crew compartments. The Apes then use principle of motion and materialise to gank every single trooper at once, whether they're in a vehicle or not.<br /> <br /> Then they do this four more times.<br /> <br /> The soldiers don't get a chance to shoot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T13:07:23-07:00","id":1345034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345029#post1345029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, the best way to deal with this is to arm the blood apes. Give them body armour, giant shotguns, and top hats and pinstripe suits, and the playing field will be levelled.<br /> <br /> Edit: and oh yeah. The salvation war? Really? You're using that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where is the Twilight getting these &quot;giant shotguns&quot;? Or body armor?<br /> <br /> Besides, body armor means fuck-all against a SAW. Or a medium machine gun. Or an autocannon. Or a tank cannon. Or artillery.<br /> <br /> And Salvation War isn't any less ridiculous than half the ideas I see posted on this forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T13:08:06-07:00","id":1345035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345033#post1345033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read it. Not impressed.<br /> <br /> 2000 of the Blood Apes walk, Immaterial into Close range of the soldiers. The soldiers smell rotten meat and hear gnashing of teeth -- maybe a few of them fire bullets into the air. The Blood Apes literally walk through tank armor and into artillery crew compartments. The Apes then use principle of motion and materialise to gank every single trooper at once, whether they're in a vehicle or not.<br /> <br /> Then they do this four more times.<br /> <br /> The soldiers don't get a chance to shoot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. And that's not all. People have literally written demons that are memetic Seals. Demons with dematerialize and basic charms for stealth and excellencies can beat the shit out of any kind of mortal force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T13:11:27-07:00","id":1345037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345034#post1345034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Where is the Twilight getting these &amp;quot;giant shotguns&amp;quot;? Or body armor?<br /> <br /> Besides, body armor means fuck-all against a SAW. Or a medium machine gun. Or an autocannon. Or a tank cannon. Or artillery.<br /> <br /> And Salvation War isn't any less ridiculous than half the ideas I see posted on this forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be absurd. <br /> <br /> Ignoring your view of warfare as some kind of rts game, salvation war was written by a hack.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's hilarious. He made demons allergic to Iron... So they'll be stuck in bronze age warfare. He made them have fire blood... So they die if they get a paper cut. And somehow, despite having access to the afterlife, they have no idea of the accomplishments and advancement of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T13:28:07-07:00","id":1345041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345037#post1345037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't be absurd.<br /> <br /> Ignoring your view of warfare as some kind of rts game, salvation war was written by a hack.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's hilarious. He made demons allergic to Iron... So they'll be stuck in bronze age warfare. He made them have fire blood... So they die if they get a paper cut. And somehow, despite having access to the afterlife, they have no idea of the accomplishments and advancement of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Don't be absurd.&quot;<br /> <br /> Rich<br /> <br /> &quot;Ignoring your view of warfare as some kind of rts game&quot;<br /> <br /> Explain, <i><b><u>in detail</u></b></i>, where I implied any such nonsense. Do modern armies not make use of combined arms, small-unit tactics, or in-depth strategic planning, now?<br /> <br /> &quot;He made demons allergic to Iron&quot;<br /> <br /> So Exalteds Raksha having <i>the same exact weakness</i> is just..... okay, in your book? Hmm.<br /> <br /> &quot; He made them have fire blood... So they die if they get a paper cut&quot;<br /> <br /> IIRC, only the flying ones have that, and that is rather-explictly so they follow the laws of physics.<br /> <br /> &quot;And somehow, despite having access to the afterlife, they have no idea of the accomplishments and advancement of humanity.&quot;<br /> <br /> I like how you miss the fact that the Demons (and Angels, for that matter) think they are so far above humanity that <i><b>they don't care</b></i> about humanities accomplishments, until they start getting ROFLstomped, and the more forward-thinking Demons take to learning as much about humanity as they can. And you are ignoring the fact that they <i>do</i> check on humanity regularly....... by the standards of immortal beings. It is very hard to fully explain just how quickly humanity has advanced in <i><b><u>just 500 years</u></b></i>. 1000 AD isnt all <i>that </i>much different from 2000 BC when you get down to the nitty gritty, while 2000 AD is <i><b><u> very</u></b></i> different from 1000 AD.<br /> <br /> And. again, the basis of Salvation War is <i>far</i> from the most ridiculous thing, especially for some of the stuff I have read <u><i>on this very forum</i></u>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T13:44:01-07:00","id":1345045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345041#post1345041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Don't be absurd.&quot;<br /> <br /> Rich<br /> <br /> &quot;Ignoring your view of warfare as some kind of rts game&quot;<br /> <br /> Explain, <i><b><u>in detail</u></b></i>, where I implied any such nonsense. Do modern armies not make use of combined arms, small-unit tactics, or in-depth strategic planning, now?<br /> <br /> &amp;</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine. I'll humour you on this one. <br /> <br /> Warfare is 90 percent boredom. 10 percent terror. You have a bunch of barracks, and your troops sleep in it. A few hundred or so. Troops don't sleep with their guns next to them. Unlike movies. So in the dead of night, a few hundred blood apes come in, and tear them to pieces. Principle of motion and bane weapon and increased strength means that for that terrifying 30 seconds where no one knows what the fuck is happening, each blood ape kills... A dozen men. <br /> <br /> Alright. Fine. So they take turns. Guards right there, standing guard over the sleeping soldiers. But that has problems. Ignoring the morale issues of realising that the monsters can kill them in their sleep, armed soldiers do not put people at ease. And that's ignoring the fact that if the blood apes attack again, those guards armed with assault rifles are going to go through friendly fire. Especially if they use grenades. <br /> <br /> So fine. <br /> <br /> Artillery is done via vehicles and driving around a car with a big gun attached to it. Our driver is pushing it around, yawning from poor sleep, waiting for the monsters to come, when he hears a growl beside him. His eyes widen and he reaches for his pistol. His throat is torn out. The blood ape presses the gas pedal and chucks the artillery piece over the cliff or crashes it into the motor pool. This continues onwards. Guys stuck in a tank? Blood ape appears. Principle of motion and a cramped space turns it into a slaughter. Guy in a support vehicle? Dies. Maybe he can get on or two shots off, but the bloodaped are furious, violent, and soak with full stamina and don't bleed.<br /> <br /> So on and so forth. <br /> <br /> And them there's support staff. 90 percent of an army doesn't fight. They cook. They run communications and encryption. They drive. They do paperwork. They maintain equipment. <br /> <br /> And they can't fight off a blood ape that's decided to kill them. Unless you're posting several armed soldiers per support personnel, you're going to get losses.<br /> <br /> Then there's the healing. Blood apes do aggravated damage to mortals and have high dice pools. They hit someone? That person is down for the count for months or years. Blood apes are spirits. They soak with full stamina and don't bleed and have exalted healing. Beat a blood ape to within an inch of his life and he'll come back up in a month at most. Your guys? Not so much.<br /> <br /> 10, 000 blood apes aren't going to march in rank and file for your artillery and machine guns and autocannoms to fire on. They're going to use their dematerialization and spirit nature to carry out constant hit and run attacks, striking at vital machinery and personnel. Always dictating the terms of engagement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 10-31-2019, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T14:39:24-07:00","id":1345065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345045#post1345045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -stuff n things.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Fine. I'll humour you on this one.&quot;<br /> <br /> Oh, <i>thank you, your Grace</i> /s Way to ensure I never read anything else of yours again.<br /> <br /> Are you mixing 2E and 3E together into nonsense again, Accelerator?<br /> <br /> &quot;bane weapon&quot;<br /> <br /> Isnt in the Blood Ape section of the 3E book. In fact, a search of &quot;bane weapon&quot; of the entire 3E book brings up nothing of the sort. If you have something that says otherwise, post it please<br /> <br /> &quot;Blood apes do aggravated damage to mortals&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, not in the 3E book. If you have something that says otherwise, post it please<br /> <br /> &quot;and have high dice pools&quot;<br /> <br /> Not really, mate. Going by the 3E QC stats, average mortal soldiers arent <i>that</i> far behind a Blood Ape, and can make up the difference with some decent Command actions.<br /> <br /> &quot;soak with full stamina&quot;<br /> <br /> According to the 3E QC stats, mortal soldiers in armor have a higher Soak than Blood Apes, which is kinda funny<br /> <br /> &quot; and don't bleed.&quot;<br /> <br /> Neither do Exalts, and yet turning their insides into their outsides tends to kill them pretty dead, all things considered. My <i>mortal players</i> have killed Exalts, Undead, minor Fae and Demons, with spears and arrows.<br /> <br /> &quot;Beat a blood ape to within an inch of his life and he'll come back up in a month at most&quot;<br /> <br /> Doesn't really matter. The Blood Apes won't be coming back if the soldiers put a bullet in the chest of the summoner.<br /> <br /> Regardless, we are done here. Lets get back to whatever the hell the actual topic of this thread was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T14:57:18-07:00","id":1345066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345065#post1345065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, we are done here. Lets get back to whatever the hell the actual topic of this thread was.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty much just this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T15:08:21-07:00","id":1345073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345066#post1345066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty much just this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. <br /> <br /> Do you guys get annoyed that I talk so much? <br /> <br /> I've been pretty excited about the whole concept of 'exaltation in other settings' for awhile, and so I've been talking a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T15:29:59-07:00","id":1345079,"title":"","content":"It's the thread you started, talk away. Obviously that's not the same as people agreeing with everything you say, clearly they don't, but I don't think you making lots of posts is an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T15:49:57-07:00","id":1345085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345073#post1345073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah.<br /> <br /> Do you guys get annoyed that I talk so much?<br /> <br /> I've been pretty excited about the whole concept of 'exaltation in other settings' for awhile, and so I've been talking a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talking is fine, just try to avoid slipping into a dismissive attitude when people disagree with you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T19:40:19-07:00","id":1345144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1345079#post1345079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the thread you started, talk away. Obviously that's not the same as people agreeing with everything you say, clearly they don't, but I don't think you making lots of posts is an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, fine. <br /> <br /> Well, I got a pet project. It's not very well done, but its something close to my heart. <br /> <br /> The first time I ever read an LN was when I picked up a few novels by the name of Campione! from baka-tsuki. Campione is basically a setting where gods from the realm of myth and legend descend onto the mortal world. Bad news. Entering the mortal material realm apparently sends these highly spiritual beings berserk, turning them insane and either apathetic to mortal life at best or just plain malicious. What's worse is that their sheer power means that they cause chaos and destruction wherever they go, war gods causing strife and sun gods causing drought, etc. <br /> <br /> Mortals in this place can use magic to enhance themselves to the level of first circle demons, and with a lot of effort, be able to launch 2nd-circle leve attacks once or twice. But in the face of literal gods, they fall back. The gods aren't like the bureaucratic field gods in Creation. These gods are approximately on the level of 2nd to 3rd circle demons, with the very strongest capable of wrecking entire cities in a matter of moments. What's worse is the existence of 'tiers'. In game terms, whenever a mortal fires out a magical attack at a divine being, they basically get a massive penalty on the effect, with lower effects simply not working and stronger ones greatly weakened.<br /> <br /> The only people who can fight off these gods are Campione. People who by luck or by pure insanity managed to kill off a god, and via an old ritual, automatically get a portion of their powers. Problem. These are humans, by all standards, and getting god-like powers isn't helping. And it also gets worse since for a human to try and fight a deity means there is something really 'off' about him. Or at least, abnormal by human standards. Even the most benign and benelovent Campione constantly risks wiping out the human race via temporal paradoxes or destroys one famous world heritage site in every single volume. <br /> <br /> In other words, humans are fucked, they're helpless against the gods/ campiones, and all the magical organisations can do is just flee, serve them as best as they can, or just try and redirect their attention. <br /> <br /> The light novel itself isn't very good. Bland protag, standard tropes, harem... its basically a cut above the rest, but there's nothing special about it. At least, not compared to Re zero. But, eh, it was the gateway for Light Novels to me, and I think I should write a story about them. <br /> <br /> So there are a bunch of characters. The main MC is one, but let's not talk about him, because he's bland as fuck. Instead, let's talk about 2 people! Or at least, 1. Erica Blandelli, basically the one who dragged the MC into the world of magic by pure accident. Child prodigy, who managed to at 16 years of age reach a position of power and skill most grown men don't reach in their 30s. Skilled fighter, highly intelligent, highly determined... and she's also refreshingly direct. No hopping about and stuttering about feelings and shit. She just comes up, wham, bam, and walks through to get what she wants. That includes using superstrength and mind control. She's partnered with her friend, Lilianna. Similarly skilled, but far less direct, more shy, and whatnot. Friends since childhood, and having a bond that's somewhere between enemies and close friends and rivals. <br /> <br /> Erica's a blonde. Liliana has silver hair. I think you know what's happening. <br /> <br /> So obviously, we have a chance for a solar-lunar bond thing here. I haven't gotten Fangs at the gate yet (not sure if its worth it) but I'm fairly sure that a solar-lunar combo with a supernal in at least a combat ability lets them fire out bullcrap that, if it cannot outright slay a third circle level being, can at least drive it off or make it think twice before fucking with them. And then there's the training they can carry out... I would like to see a political fic where they decide to rally the men around them, and drive off at least one or two gods and kill them, with the god's death being the equivalent of 'getting lots of xp'. <br /> <br /> Of course, that can be boring. For instance, another idea would be an infernal exalted appearing. Mortals always fight the gods, the campiones, and the divine beasts they unleash... but being mortals, they just fail. Their spells die, their swords break, and their bodies are broken. The campione or god simply laughs, slays their loved ones, and walks off, content and confident in their power. No one can stop them... unless offered power. I mean, let's be goddamned honest here. Anybody would take the power to just, well, not get beaten down by the divine asshats that roam the earth. At which point, whether Malfean wrath, Cecylenian manipulation, or just plain ass combination of all so they can fight off the gods rampaging across the earth. Lots of people are willing to give up everything, just for a chance to fight the gods. And I'm fiarly sure that Malfeas and his ilk will be willing to help. Not to mention an Abyssal Exaltation works just as well. Someone slain by the casual backhand of a campione or Heretic god, and comes back to haunt them, fighting and hunting them down again and again, until the campione is crippled and weakened and just dies. <br /> <br /> Then there's another idea. Alchemical exalted. <br /> <br /> The magic organisations of the world are powerful, mighty, and incredibly influential. They command vast resources, millions of supersoldiers, magic that congress would give up its right eye for, wealth to beggar nations, and even more magical artifacts and mystic lore. The problem is that campiones and gods are so insanely powerful, that all this is useless. Dozens of the world's greatest magi working together might disrupt a campione if he's particularly distracted. Armies of supersoldiers die to greater-scale magics. All the money, all the resources in the world, can't make a dent in the face of divine opposition. And so, the problem is turning that money and power into something that can face the divine head on and win. <br /> <br /> Enter the Alchemical exalted. Alchemical exalted need many things. Magical materials. Specialised clay. Entire teams of specialists. A heroic soul. And the approval of Autochthon himself. Now since we're writing a story, we can homebrew some shit so that they somehow get it. Maybe a divine revelation from one of their precogs and priestesses. Maybe a discovery of a cache, with it being labelled as a superweapon. But either way, they don't have much to lose. I mean, an entire nation could build an alchemical exalted, and there's nothing saying that the magical organisations can't do the same. Alchemical exalted can be described as an aircraft carrier or an ICBM. A piece of technomagical artistry that is built by a nation or state to serve its needs. <br /> <br /> The organizations work together, pooling resources and setting up secret meetings. Trawling through the underworld and taking what they can find. Searching old mystic lore, digging up old sites, sacrificing age old relics for the needed materials, devoting the time and energy of thousands of their own experts to build this possible new... weapon. <br /> <br /> The newcomer is less than stellar, and some lose heart. But others, realize what is happening. There is a spark of the divine here. By this time, all he has is excellencies, but that can soon change. New designs, new ideas, new charms... all there. Something reached through and empowered this... automaton, giving it power and ability when before it should simply be a pile of clay and expensive materials. More is added. The first one is not meant for combat, but instead for thinking. It is meant to build more of its own kind, to marshall resources to build even more charms and alchemicals. Slowly, ever so slowly, the Assembly is built, one by one... <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T02:45:33-08:00","id":1351618,"title":"","content":"I think it would be pretty great if Exaltations showed up in DC comics at the moment. The current major cosmic crisis involves Perpetua, the mother of the Monitor and the Anti-Monitor as well as their brother the World Forger, trying to harness the psychic energy of humans in a philosophy called &quot;Doom&quot; which is essentially social darwinism through the lens of supervillainy to transform the DC multiverse into it's stronger, eternal form with which she can challenge her own race of multiverse-creating cosmic deities. To do this she transformed Lex Luthor into a primordial human from the template she made in the very first version of reality by giving him technology to absorb Martian Manhunter, leaving him looking like a cross between Perfect Cell and Majin Buu. He then formed the Legion of Doom you might recognise from the DC Animated Universe, and went on a quest to give everyone on Earth presents at a time when the Justice League was coming under fire for accidentally cracking a hole in the multiverse while chaining up Barbatos: The cosmic bat-god who had been using nightmare versions of Batman made of dark matter (Shadow Slave Extraction, anyone?) to sink the positive matter portion of the multiverse into the Dark Multiverse beneath it.<br /> <br /> In the comic the Justice League has been caught flatfooted due to, largely, underestimating the Legion of Doom. So I think Clark becoming a Zenith, Bruce becoming a Night, Diana becoming a Dawn, Barry becoming an Eclipse and Cyborg becoming a Twilight would give them the edge and awareness to respond quicker and fight on more of an even keel instead of being repeatedly outplanned. I see Arthur Curry as more of a Full Moon Lunar, and Kendra (Hawkgirl) currently has an arc where it is discovered that she is supposed to become the current version of reality's cosmic bird of prey to stop Perpetua (a previous one created the Source Wall originally to seal away Perpetua and her army of human-martian hybrids) so I'd say she'd make a good No Moon. J'onn (Martian Manhunter) himself is an interesting case because the current plot has him being Luthor's forgotten childhood friend which Luthor is conflicted about absorbing for power after recovering his memories while also being in a relationship with Hawkgirl, so I also see him as a Changing Moon Lunar. <br /> <br /> Not all villains have thrown in with Perpetua, and I think it's the more independant ones that would likely earn the other Exaltations. Grail would be a prime Scourge. Mister Thunderbolt could be a Chosen of Secrets since he has the secret of the H-Dial. Black Adam and the Marvel Family are, in many ways, already DC's version of Exigents which is awkward because while a lot of gods would likely want them as their chosen DC deities being Manichean-style self aware ideas whose true forms exist outside the infinite physical dimensions within the Sphere of the Gods mean the Exigence bestower would likely try to sell them on exotic, novel powers since they largely specialise in Superman-like raw power on top of great magical potential. Controller Mu strikes me as a villainous Twilight, and while I'm not sure what Darkseid would be he's probably disqualified from Exaltation by being a god, even in broken aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T02:03:27-08:00","id":1351813,"title":"","content":"I've always wanted to see exaltations reach other settings... and touch the villains. <br /> <br /> Two-bit villain, defeated in the first 20 chapters of the story? His life ruined and himself a laughing stock? His family destroyed, like that of the ones in a Xianxia novel? <br /> <br /> Well, an infernal exaltation comes up, knocking on his door, saying that they're willing to give him power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T22:51:59-08:00","id":1351970,"title":"","content":"Also, I\u2019d now like to see a setting where Exalted are either by default underdogs Becuase of all the crazy shit running around, or just are a mildly unsusul but not overwhelmly addition to the verse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T01:32:09-08:00","id":1351980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kalzky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1351970#post1351970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I\u2019d now like to see a setting where Exalted are either by default underdogs Becuase of all the crazy shit running around, or just are a mildly unsusul but not overwhelmly addition to the verse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends greatly on the setting and what it's like. Depends on how much the Exalted can grab and reverse engineer. <br /> <br /> This includes The Culture, Nobilis, Mage the Ascension, Saint Seiya, and what else.<br /> <br /> The problem, of course, comes when the Exalted begin to adapt to whatever is hitting them and start stealing stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T03:22:56-08:00","id":1351986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1351980#post1351980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends greatly on the setting and what it's like. Depends on how much the Exalted can grab and reverse engineer. <br /> <br /> This includes The Culture, Nobilis, Mage the Ascension, Saint Seiya, and what else.<br /> <br /> The problem, of course, comes when the Exalted begin to adapt to whatever is hitting them and start stealing stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of the games I actually know...I mean, we have books for Mage crossover. But Noblis?<br /> Noblis is outside their pay grade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T03:33:54-08:00","id":1351989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kalzky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1351986#post1351986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of the games I actually know...I mean, we have books for Mage crossover. But Noblis?<br /> Noblis is outside their pay grade.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I can tell? Oh, most definitely. Completely and utterly outside. There are, like, tiers. Exalted are pretty cool and dangerous. But the Nobilis are waaaayyy too hax. <br /> <br /> But another idea is Orion's arm. Archailects should be a pretty nice thing to throw at the Exalted host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T04:51:34-08:00","id":1351994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kalzky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1351970#post1351970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I\u2019d now like to see a setting where Exalted are either by default underdogs Becuase of all the crazy shit running around, or just are a mildly unsusul but not overwhelmly addition to the verse.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would definitely be the case in DC if the Exaltations went to street level heroes like Green Arrow and Black Canary instead of ones like Superman who literaly punched over a being that forges entire multiverses recently. Although DC can be very odd about the empowered. An old comic implied superheroes where Aquaman traveled into a magical ocean reflecting the collective unconsciousness implied superheroes a whole were supplanting the gods of the modern era, and Batman is sort of like the Gorol of DC because while until recently he was portrayed as a &quot;peak human&quot;, the Dark Nights Metal arc revealed his victories were orchestrated by the cosmic bat-god that ate the multiverse creator from above. That entity in turn only saw Batman because Darkseid's Omega Sanction hurled him back in time to retroactively fill his life with all the suffering up until then and prime him as a time bomb for the present. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T04:57:47-08:00","id":1351995,"title":"","content":"Urgh, no. Not DC or Marvel. <br /> <br /> Those universes are so goddamned weird.<br /> <br /> Like, seriously. Can a twilight take over the place, and start churning Reed Richard's level of tech? Can they use their social skills to sway over entire countries to their will? Will the heroes stop them, despite them not using any form of mind control? There are technology that gives people their powers. Can the exalted take the tech, reverse engineer them, then make artifact versions to beat them up? Can they learn magic, and apply their occult excellency to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T06:13:31-08:00","id":1352006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1351995#post1351995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Urgh, no. Not DC or Marvel.<br /> <br /> Those universes are so goddamned weird.<br /> <br /> Like, seriously. Can a twilight take over the place, and start churning Reed Richard's level of tech? Can they use their social skills to sway over entire countries to their will? Will the heroes stop them, despite them not using any form of mind control? There are technology that gives people their powers. Can the exalted take the tech, reverse engineer them, then make artifact versions to beat them up? Can they learn magic, and apply their occult excellency to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I have some doubts about DC because according to Final Crisis <i>the entire multiverse is a kind of self-refining story that makes Superman win no matter what</i><i>, even when up against cosmic beings that are essentially author self-inserts</i>, according to Dark Nights metal <u>everything contains trace components of a cosmic metal that makes the Magical Materials of Exalted look redundant because it embodies pure possibility even on the level of restoring the entire multiverse from the brink of destruction when channeled correctly</u> and according to Doomsday Clock <b>even a reality warper stronger than the strongest imagination dimension imp Mr. Mxyptik trying to interfere with it's history will invite violent retaliation from Superman</b>. The most recent Justice League run outright confirms it was intended as an eternal, human-martian hybrid dominated, supervillain social darwinism-powered superweapon by the Anti-Monitor and Monitor's mother.<br /> <br /> That said, I think a Twilight could easily take over Marvel for a number of reasons. For one thing Secret Wars showed that Doctors Doom and Strange alone were able to defeat the Beyonders, beings from outside the Marvel multiverse who destroyed all of it's Abstracts including the Living Tribunal. They did this basically using a tip from Molecule Man, building a bomb made out of his clones by abusing the fact the Beyonders are linearly restricted in time and so <b>can't sense time travel even though they can murder the personification of time with big lasers (?!?!?!?!?!)</b>, and since <b>they are both merely humans who studied science and magic very hard</b> in theory Twilight could have done everything they did but better. For another, in Starlin's The Infinity Ending Thanos recently<b><i><u> murdered the Living Tribunal and The One Above All (as in the being formerly defined as both the one true God, implied to be the avatar of Marvel's writers AND WITH THANOS USING HIS POWERS PROVEN CAPABLE OF ENCOMPASSING THE ACTUAL, REAL LIFE READERS INTO HIS BEING</u></i></b> by abusing the fact Death essentially friendzoned him so hard he counted as not being part of reality to steal one of the OAA's anchors used to keep different multiverses apart, then use it to absorb other Cosmic Abstracts such as Galactus, Master Order and Eternity, which destabilised <b>the structured system the OAA is dependant on to be supreme in Marvel</b> and allowed him to absorb them both and gain all their powers. It's worth noting in the story that Thanos' prowess in science, magic and so on were utterly irrelevant to simply finding out about the anchors and using them. In other words, the fact that the Exaltation (or you hypothetical Twilight) presumably comes from outside of the Marvel multiverse alone gives them an immense advantage over the entire Marvel multiverse by making them elligible to do exactly what Thanos did to absorb The One Above All.<br /> <br /> tl;dr Marvel is absurdly self-destructive and open to abuse for a theoretically powerful setting while DC seems to be undergoing the multiversal equivalent of Luna's Cthonic Baara.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T09:59:21-08:00","id":1352025,"title":"","content":"See? This is what I meant. I turn my back on marvel and dc for five minutes, and this happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T11:20:16-08:00","id":1352184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1352025#post1352025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See? This is what I meant. I turn my back on marvel and dc for five minutes, and this happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I turned my back on them forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T12:34:34-08:00","id":1355466,"title":"","content":"To me, the far more concerning thing about superhero media - Marvel <i>and</i> DC - seems to be the relatively consistent message that rocking the boat <i>makes </i>you a bad person, even if the boat is absolutely awful.<br /> <br /> \u200bGotham is an absolute <i>hole</i>, and everyone who tries to clean things up and isn't named &quot;Bruce Wayne&quot; either is revealed to be a villain, or ends up becoming one. (And for all the millions that Bruce Wayne has supposedly spent on improving Gotham, it's <i>still</i> a hole.)<br /> <br /> Reed Richards has a cure for cancer, but he refuses to share it, because &quot;we're not ready yet&quot;; scientists who actually <i>try</i> and make things better end up getting corrupted by their experiments and mutate into monsters, or have to rob banks to fund their research.<br /> <br /> It seems the primary way you can have power and be a good person in superhero fiction is to either be born with it or acquire it entirely by chance, and then only fight to keep things pretty much the same - if you work to acquire your power or try to use your power to change things, there's a good chance that you're a morally reprehensible person.<br /> <br /> Is this surprising to see a message like that being amplified by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Walt_Disney_Company\" target=\"_blank\">a company that owns 40% of the world's entertainment?</a> Probably not. Is it still a problem? Oh, hell yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-17-2019, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T12:53:19-08:00","id":1355469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355466#post1355466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this surprising to see a message like that coming from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Walt_Disney_Company\" target=\"_blank\">a company that owns 40% of the world's entertainment?</a> Probably not. Is it still a problem? Oh, hell yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It probably contributes to why Western comics are dying and more Americans are buying manga.<br /> <br /> Most manga tells a story with an end, and even the longest running ones will die when the author does. You can tell a story about a hero who actually changes their world.<br /> <br /> Some franchises (Gundam, Macross, Pretty Cure) keep themselves going through sequels, beginning with a new start and progressing to a new end. Sometimes they use completely new casts of characters, or completely different continuities.<br /> <br /> And there are more options than &quot;masked vigilante who achieves justice by acting outside of the law; breaking and entering, spying, theft, kidnapping, assault, traffic violations, property damage, manslaughter, etc... with no accountability.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;You can only change the world by being the most powerful person ever&quot; is certainly a complaint I've seen levied against Captain Marvel and Rey in the new Star Wars.<br /> <br /> They don't struggle, they don't fail, they don't win by being clever or morally good.<br /> <br /> Luke ran like a bitch from Vader in the first movie, got his ass kicked and his hand cut off in the second, and could only beat Vader in the third by giving into the dark side. Which he stopped doing, winning the moral victory, which convinced his father to repent. He took his lumps, he grew up from being a whiny farmboy, he learned, and he still won without strength.<br /> <br /> Boys wanted to be Luke because he showed them they can start as childish farmboys and become heroic men. Han Solo was popular too, because he was a loser with a dirty van and a pistol who became a war hero.<br /> <br /> Rey defeats the most powerful warrior in the galaxy in her first movie, and she beats Ben every single time they fight. He's no Vader, and she's no Luke. No one can watch her and feel like they can become her too, except the people who were already convinced they were the most amazing person in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-17-2019, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T13:09:36-08:00","id":1355473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355466#post1355466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, the far more concerning thing about superhero media - Marvel <i>and</i> DC - seems to be the relatively consistent message that rocking the boat <i>makes </i>you a bad person, even if the boat is absolutely awful.<br /> <br /> \u200bGotham is an absolute <i>hole</i>, and everyone who tries to clean things up and isn't named &amp;quot;Bruce Wayne&amp;quot; either is revealed to be a villain, or ends up becoming one.<br /> <br /> Reed Richards has a cure for cancer, but he refuses to share it, because &amp;quot;we're not ready yet&amp;quot;; scientists who actually <i>try</i> and make things better end up getting corrupted by their experiments and mutate into monsters, or have to rob banks to fund their research.<br /> <br /> It seems the primary way you can have power and be a good person in superhero fiction is to either be born with it or acquire it entirely by chance, and then only fight to keep things pretty much the same - if you work to acquire your power or try to use your power to change things, there's a good chance that you're a morally reprehensible person.<br /> <br /> Is this surprising to see a message like that coming from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Walt_Disney_Company\" target=\"_blank\">a company that owns 40% of the world's entertainment?</a> Probably not. Is it still a problem? Oh, hell yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a problem before Disney and is a result of the medium trying to stay in a recognizable reality for children and not spiral off into Science Fiction. If Reed Richards can cure cancer, solve the global energy crisis and all that then the setting moves farther and farther from the mainline\u2014that and the comics cannot end, for a variety of reasons. Disney benefits but didn\u2019t invent the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T13:18:43-08:00","id":1355475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355473#post1355473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disney benefits but didn\u2019t invent the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but by not changing the message when they adapted the Marvel universe to the big screen, I'd argue that Disney's perpetuation of the message verbatim makes them at least somewhat responsible for its place in the mainstream.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Also, the superhero universes' attempts to remain &quot;in a recognizable reality&quot; makes them <i>even weirder</i> - the fact that Tony Stark has these fantastical holographic computers that are controlled with hand gestures and voice commands all the way back in 2008, and folks are still just getting regular-ass Mac computers at the Apple store when Steve Rogers pops by one in 2014, makes the setting that much more jarring. The DCEU's Earth got openly attacked by city-destroying costumed aliens <i>three times in three years</i>, why are you journalists acting like the guy who believes in Atlantis is so weird?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-17-2019, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T13:47:45-08:00","id":1355481,"title":"","content":"Overall, my point is, I like that Exalted gives the players permission - encourages them, even - to step up and shake the pillars of Heaven, and that's what sets it apart from superhero fiction to me.<br /> <br /> Being willing to change the world doesn't always make you a good person, no, but it sure as hell doesn't always make you a bad one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T14:06:46-08:00","id":1355489,"title":"","content":"Re; Sundar and Alucard's comment, I don't know about the contrast between popularity of manga and American comics (I mean, could be right, maybe not - I wouldn't really know!). Fully do get the impression from little samples that a lot of American superhero comics (possibly unrepresentative samples!) do go in weird places as narratives from this frame of being oriented around conflicts between extremely super-powerful long established characters who can't really die or change or change their world, or even really change each other. <br /> <br /> It seems like you often have these long &quot;epic&quot; overblown fight scenes interspersed with a long accompanying monologue that either expresses what a character *means* to the author (Superman expressing his Superman-ness, etc.) or serves as an excuse for an author to expound on their own personal philosophical musings on the nature of X (life, humanity, 'the Good and the Evil', parenthood, dignity and triumph in the face of adversity, etc). For several pages of panels.<br /> <br /> It seems then like sometimes this does not really accompany *any* idea of what purpose this character or conflict really serves or means in a wider story where the author really has something to say subtly through subtext and themes (rather than just shouting or preaching their ideas at you through a monologue!). Rather it just serves to express the character's brand personality, or it serves as an blood pumping epic conflict accompanied by an often feel good &quot;totally awesome Fuck Yeah!&quot; speech or supposedly profound sermon for a quick endorphin rush.<br /> <br /> But then, this seems like a constraint of characters and plots having to be these eternal, unchanging monetized brand icons. It doesn't seem like necessarily a constraint of making modern day stories about super powered people who want to achieve things in their world, or even lots of the particular tropes of the particular US comic book incarnation of this idea.<br /> <br /> So going back to the specific point about heroes who do or don't change the world, I'd say from my perspective it's totally fine to make stories about heroes who don't. Maybe this is because the author is making an argument that powerful supermen shouldn't change the world, and maybe the subtext is because this is the author trying to avoid certain ideas about authoritarian and elitist minorities imposing radical ideas on society through force, or because they want to explore grounded stories that stick with the world as we know it. Or it's some other reason. However, whatever the reason, ideally that should be because <i>that's the story the author wants to tell, </i>sincerely, and should not have the issue that the audience can't really believe them because they know that this is hollow and the storyteller is ultimately just motivated by keeping the world of the story intact in order to sell it again in the future.<br /> <br /> (So possibly this is either me just figuratively shouting at a cloud, or tl;dr-ing on the value of sincerity in expression over commercial constraints. But it was fun to write!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T14:26:52-08:00","id":1355496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355489#post1355489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re; Sundar and Alucard's comment, I don't know about the contrast between popularity of manga and American comics...</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say anything about manga or Star Wars, please don't put me into that camp.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355489#post1355489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe this is because the author is making an argument that powerful supermen shouldn't change the world...</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's not <i>just </i>supermen who the movies are telling it's not okay to want to change the world - it's the little guys, people like you and me. &quot;Ambition is evil,&quot; these narratives say, &quot;and <i>you </i>should only wield power if you were born with it or get it by accident.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T14:52:13-08:00","id":1355500,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a>, sorry if I attached bits of Sunder's post to you by accident. I'm kind of assuming anyone reading my post read at least three or four posts up and would know which bits were your argument and which were his.<br /> <br /> Re; &quot;ambition is evil&quot; and narrative that suggest super-people shouldn't change the world suggesting no one should try and enact positive change, it seems like that depends on how the author is handling the topic. I'm only giving one example of what an author might be trying to express. I don't really have a strong stance on whether stories featuring superheroes should have them changing the world or not, in order to be successful. My argument here is more that whatever the author is expressing, let her audience believe she's expressing it sincerely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T15:14:52-08:00","id":1355502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355500#post1355500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a>, sorry if I attached bits of Sunder's post to you by accident. I'm kind of assuming anyone reading my post read at least three or four posts up and would know which bits were your argument and which were his.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given various arguments that have been attributed to me in the past, I'm not always willing to roll those dice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355500#post1355500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re; &quot;ambition is evil&quot; and narrative that suggest super-people shouldn't change the world suggesting no one should try and enact positive change, it seems like that depends on how the author is handling the topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just the writers. We've also got editors, artists, and of course executives all tweaking things.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Dark Phoenix Saga has a pretty good example of how authorial intent can get mangled before we readers ever see it. The writers did not intend for Jean Grey to die, but because <i>the artists</i> drew aliens watching in horror as she destroyed their sun, the executives forced the writers to kill her off.<br /> <br /> \u200bDC had a planned story arc in which one of their heroes would become a despotic villain in the future, but when fans guessed the despot's identity they changed it on the fly.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's <i>quite a lot</i> of meddling in the superhero industry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-17-2019, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T17:13:29-08:00","id":1355519,"title":"","content":"One of the things I like the most about exalted is how the power chooses people. You know how they always say that the appearance of superheroes would lead to governments forming agencies, and the superheroes working for them for a paycheck?<br /> <br /> Yeah, this ain't happening now. Like it or not, exaltation goes to someone who would use the power. For good or ill. And they're not the kind of people who can just be bribed away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T17:57:37-08:00","id":1355537,"title":"","content":"Well, depends on how convincing their arguments are; I\u2019ve said it before, I\u2019ll say it again, if this inviolable sense of self/purpose were so fundamental to the Exalted, the game wouldn\u2019t have an Integrity Ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T18:24:40-08:00","id":1355543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355537#post1355537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, depends on how convincing their arguments are; I\u2019ve said it before, I\u2019ll say it again, if this inviolable sense of self/purpose were so fundamental to the Exalted, the game wouldn\u2019t have an Integrity Ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I guess so. But I mean, how many exalts can you actually bribe to not be completely disruptive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T18:32:24-08:00","id":1355548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355543#post1355543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. I guess so. But I mean, how many exalts can you actually bribe to not be completely disruptive?</div> </div> </div> </div>What\u2019s their Resolve? What are their Intimacies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T19:05:13-08:00","id":1355555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355548#post1355548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s their Resolve? What are their Intimacies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno. <br /> <br /> Just what kind of people are chosen as exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T19:59:14-08:00","id":1355566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355555#post1355555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just what kind of people are chosen as exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite a few. Poets and historians, surgeons and sailors, thieves and killers, princes and prostitutes, smiths and savants, monks and madmen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T20:07:12-08:00","id":1355568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355566#post1355566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite a few. Poets and historians, surgeons and sailors, thieves and killers, princes and prostitutes, smiths and savants, monks and madmen.</div> </div> </div> </div>The kinds of people who are willing to use the power. And enact great change in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T20:13:36-08:00","id":1355570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355475#post1355475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b(Also, the superhero universes' attempts to remain &quot;in a recognizable reality&quot; makes them <i>even weirder</i> - the fact that Tony Stark has these fantastical holographic computers that are controlled with hand gestures and voice commands all the way back in 2008, and folks are still just getting regular-ass Mac computers at the Apple store when Steve Rogers pops by one in 2014, makes the setting that much more jarring. The DCEU's Earth got openly attacked by city-destroying costumed aliens <i>three times in three years</i>, why are you journalists acting like the guy who believes in Atlantis is so weird?)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually a deeper problem than that because it also affects where superheroes and supervillains get their powers from. They're exceptional people that stand apart from the rest as demigods in power. Most people luck into that by birth or accident just because it's a convenient way to explain why there's only one of them instead of a whole world of them.<br /> <br /> It also makes storytelling really really really hard. Either you're Batman, and your city sucks but you're trying really hard to fix it and always seeming to fall short, because as soon as you do fix it the story is over, or you're Superman, who lives in the near utopia of Metropolis and is always defending the status quo because the status quo is awesome under the watch of the supremely powerful and benevolent hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T00:47:49-08:00","id":1355596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355568#post1355568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The kinds of people who are willing to use the power. And enact great change in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or succumb to a world that\u2019s much larger than them. Or be outfoxed by a crafty mortal. Or fall to despair at the sight of how cruel humans can be to their fellows. Or become part of the system that oppresses the people they used to be. Or remain ignorant of the problems that <i>need</i> addressing, wasting billions of dollars and man-hours on a vanity project while the world burns.<br /> <br /> The future ain\u2019t written in stone, after all, and the story is far less fun if there\u2019s no possibility for failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-18-2019, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T04:33:33-08:00","id":1355611,"title":"","content":"There's innate problems with shared universes, imagine if we had to try and reconcile all our chronicles as taking place in the same world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T05:31:41-08:00","id":1355618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355596#post1355596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or succumb to a world that\u2019s much larger than them. Or be outfoxed by a crafty mortal. Or fall to despair at the sight of how cruel humans can be to their fellows. Or become part of the system that oppresses the people they used to be. Or remain ignorant of the problems that <i>need</i> addressing, wasting billions of dollars and man-hours on a vanity project while the world burns.<br /> <br /> The future ain\u2019t written in stone, after all, and the story is far less fun if there\u2019s no possibility for failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course you can fail. Of course you can lose. But heres the thing. As long as that exalt isn't dead and refuses to give up? Then he's going to win eventually. Excellencies, charms. Longevity. And pure power assure that, if nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T07:00:22-08:00","id":1355624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355568#post1355568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The kinds of people who are willing to use the power. And enact great change in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This falls flat if it assumes that an Exalt will not think great change occurs by working with the government. There's no reason said great change can't be in line with a government or corporations plan. Why wouldn't an exalted think helping an existing power structure wouldn't be to their liking? Not all of them <i>want </i> to be kings. There's a solar working for the Prefect of Paragon, for goodness sake! Plenty of people who want to see change in the world co-operate with government and corporate powers. It's how those powers _get_ there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T07:43:11-08:00","id":1355634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355618#post1355618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course you can fail. Of course you can lose. But heres the thing. As long as that exalt isn't dead and refuses to give up? Then he's going to win eventually. Excellencies, charms. Longevity. And pure power assure that, if nothing else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily, they could just keep trying for 1,000 years making some headway and then backsliding, and going back and forth without making much progress. If the forces arrayed against them are vast enough and dedicated enough they might die of old age before completing their goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T16:56:32-08:00","id":1355720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355618#post1355618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course you can fail. Of course you can lose. But heres the thing. As long as that exalt isn't dead and refuses to give up? Then he's going to win eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet the setting still has slavery, drug addiction, cruel or indolent gods, sickness, and poverty. Do no Exalts care about these things? Or is their victory over these conditions not as inevitable after all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T17:08:55-08:00","id":1355721,"title":"","content":"There's also a big difference between specific exalts and exalts in general. A specific twilight might be able to infiltrate the global economy and manipulate it to take over the world, but a bunch of other twilights might just not be that good. Generally in Exalted the kinds of feats that your PCs can accomplish with their charms, if you try hard, represent the greatest abilities even among other Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T18:04:21-08:00","id":1355733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355543#post1355543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. I guess so. But I mean, how many exalts can you actually bribe to not be completely disruptive?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the Realm contains 15000 or so exalts, nearly all of which aren't completely disruptive.<br /> Plus Prasad and Lookshy<br /> ... at least 80%<br /> <br /> The bribe involves paying them an average person's lifetime salary every .. two months or so, but it is possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T07:25:16-08:00","id":1355838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355611#post1355611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's innate problems with shared universes, imagine if we had to try and reconcile all our chronicles as taking place in the same world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, it's hard enough just slipping in Exalts and NPCs from previous chronicles I've run as Easter eggs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T23:08:36-08:00","id":1356006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1355624#post1355624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This falls flat if it assumes that an Exalt will not think great change occurs by working with the government. There's no reason said great change can't be in line with a government or corporations plan. Why wouldn't an exalted think helping an existing power structure wouldn't be to their liking? Not all of them <i>want </i> to be kings. There's a solar working for the Prefect of Paragon, for goodness sake! Plenty of people who want to see change in the world co-operate with government and corporate powers. It's how those powers _get_ there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, to go back to the example of DC for example there's no reason an Exalt wouldn't join the Justice League if before Exalting they knew about them as the people keeping their neighbourhood safe. Not only does the JL have a crack record for taking on anyone from actual robots to the actual Wrath of God, but villains tend to be really dysfunctional and mostly held together as a group by ego and spite. Coupled with how it's recently been shown that normal DC humans such as Kamandi, Catman and Black Canary are some of the most dangerous beings in existence and capable of defeating multiverse creator killers in hand to hand combat, and being part of the JL is just plain an easier life than being in it's way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T01:43:46-08:00","id":1367446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VjQ2t_yNHQs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VjQ2t_yNHQs\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VjQ2t_yNHQs\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VjQ2t_yNHQs </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.tor.com/2010/02/03/vilcabamba/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.tor.com/2010/02/03/vilcabamba/</a><br /> <br /> I think that there's great potential here, for a dozen or so Exaltation stories to fall into an alternate earth or so, where Aliens are falling. Some dude able to jack a laptop into the Alien mothership and then send in a virus irregardless of incompatible OS and firewalls? Obviously a few solar charms. Resistance leader that is a teenager capable of leading troops against advanced alien tech? Obviously a dragonblooded general. The aliens constantly seem to have bad luck, get idiot balls, fuck up in ways that advanced civilisations usually don't, and usually just seem to be screwed at every turn? Obviously a Sidereal at work. Aliens get infiltrated? Lunars at work. <br /> <br /> Hell, being able to grab an alien spaceship, reverse engineer it, and then put the tech into your own civilisation is something I can see the Exalted doing. It's part of their schtick, after all, putting down the power bows and then taking up the laser beam cannons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T02:00:11-08:00","id":1367451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367446#post1367446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that there's great potential here, for a dozen or so Exaltation stories to fall into an alternate earth or so, where Aliens are falling. Some dude able to jack a laptop into the Alien mothership and then send in a virus irregardless of incompatible OS and firewalls? Obviously a few solar charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, bear with me here, since the alien technology fell into human hands decades back, the OS isn't incompatible because it was reverse-engineered from the alien tech? Like, <i>Independence Day</i> and Michael Bay's <i>Transformers</i> are kinda dumb in a number of regards (particularly with regard to race), but our technology being compatible with theirs because we reverse-engineered it to be, is <i>a lot more</i> sensible than having it be compatible in a world where we <i>haven't </i>had our hands on a piece of their tech for decades.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367446#post1367446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resistance leader that is a teenager capable of leading troops against advanced alien tech? Obviously a dragonblooded general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, just spitballing here, your ability to lead troops isn't strictly a factor of your age, since teenagers <i>have</i> led fights against invaders in our real-world history?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367446#post1367446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The aliens constantly seem to have bad luck, get idiot balls, fuck up in ways that advanced civilisations usually don't, and usually just seem to be screwed at every turn? Obviously a Sidereal at work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you provide me an example of a real advanced civilization that doesn't fuck up? I'm not convinced that that's a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367446#post1367446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aliens get infiltrated? Lunars at work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars lack the capacity to transform into aliens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367446#post1367446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, being able to grab an alien spaceship, reverse engineer it, and then put the tech into your own civilisation is something I can see the Exalted doing. <b>It's part of their schtick, after all, putting down the power bows and then taking up the laser beam cannons.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Whereas I see the Exalted schtick being <i>not needing to</i> put down the powerbows to fight the guys with the laser beam cannons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-13-2020, 05:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T02:10:25-08:00","id":1367455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367451#post1367451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, bear with me here, since the alien technology fell into human hands decades back, the OS isn't incompatible because it was reverse-engineered from the alien tech? Like, <i>Independence Day</i> and Michael Bay's <i>Transformers</i> are kinda dumb in a number of regards (particularly with regard to race), but our technology being compatible with theirs because we reverse-engineered it to be, is <i>a lot more</i> sensible than having it be compatible in a world where we <i>haven't </i>had our hands on a piece of their tech for decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Urm.... there's a solar lore charm that lets you connect irregardless of OS. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Or, just spitballing here, your ability to lead troops isn't strictly a factor of your age, since teenagers </span></span></span><i>have</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> led fights against invaders in our real-world history?</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to the YA tendency for teenagers to lead and do shit that no one else could do, even though lots of other guys are around that could have done what they did better. Why? Well, in this case, its because he's dragonblooded. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Can you provide me an example of a real advanced civilization that doesn't fuck up? I'm not convinced that that's a thing.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Fuck up more than usual. It's pretty hard for the British Empire to lose to natives who haven't even invented steel yet. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Lunars lack the capacity to transform into aliens.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Tell me something. Are you being purposely obtuse here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T02:38:02-08:00","id":1367460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367455#post1367455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Urm.... there's a solar lore charm that lets you connect irregardless of OS.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that. But I'm saying, at least in the context of the movies you're bringing up, is that it's not necessary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367455#post1367455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fuck up more than usual. It's pretty hard for the British Empire to lose to natives who haven't even invented steel yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Isandlwana\" target=\"_blank\">So, what, we're just going to ignore the Zulu?</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367455#post1367455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell me something. Are you being purposely obtuse here?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I am sincerely informing you that Lunars can assume human and animal shapes. They don't get to turn into aliens. I don't know that you don't know that, because you have a history of inconsistency with knowledge of the Exalted setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T02:44:13-08:00","id":1367462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367460#post1367460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Isandlwana\" target=\"_blank\">So, what, we're just going to ignore the Zulu?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I know that. That's why I said 'pretty hard'. That's not something you see everyday. <br /> <br /> British Empire failing to defeat the Zulus is kinda unusual. Usually the guys with gunpowder and steel win. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">No, I am sincerely informing you that Lunars can assume human and animal shapes. They don't get to turn into aliens. I don't know that you don't know that, because you have a history of inconsistency with knowledge of the Exalted setting.</span><br /> </span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <br /> </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Stop. Lunars can get knacks, right? Lunars can get charms to turn into trees, insects, mice, or behemoths, or demons, or fae, or ghosts, right? Or it is completely in theme for them to be able to do it, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T02:49:25-08:00","id":1367464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367462#post1367462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">British Empire failing to defeat the Zulus is kinda unusual. Usually the guys with gunpowder and steel win.</div> </div> </div> </div>History is full of nuance; it's hardly ever so simple as &quot;Who has the steel? Who has the gunpowder?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367462#post1367462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stop. Lunars can get knacks, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in 3e, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367462#post1367462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars can get charms to turn into trees, insects, mice, or behemoths, or demons, or fae, or ghosts, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only mice and insects, this time 'round. And even in editions that had Knacks, that was still something they had to develop and then buy with XP, which means it's not something you should necessarily expect a given Lunar to be capable of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T03:05:39-08:00","id":1367469,"title":"","content":"Alright, fine. I'll agree with you on the Lunars thing. I'll just leave them out of the main events. It's not like that changes anything. I'll give up on the guns and steel thing too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T03:10:17-08:00","id":1367470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367469#post1367469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, fine. I'll agree with you on the Lunars thing. I'll just leave them out of the main events.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, on the other hand, is doing a disservice to the Lunars. Just because they can't assume the shape of an alien, doesn't mean they can't serve as infiltrators. For instance, if the aliens are using human labor to mine, a Lunar could scout their asteroid base in the form of a rat or insect, and then foster an insurrection among the miners in a human shape, sharing the knowledge they gathered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367469#post1367469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like that changes anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, the problem is in the nuance you're ignoring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367469#post1367469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll give up on the guns and steel thing too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not asking you to give up; I'm asking you to <i>understand</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-13-2020, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T03:18:19-08:00","id":1367473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367470#post1367470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, on the other hand, is doing a disservice to the Lunars. Just because they can't assume the shape of an alien, doesn't mean they can't serve as infiltrators. For instance, if the aliens are using human labor to mine, a Lunar could scout their asteroid base in the form of a rat or insect, and then foster an insurrection among the miners in a human shape, sharing the knowledge they gathered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologise. I was making a joke on how Lunars in 2e tend to get a bit shafted, you know, not really doing much in the game's backstory. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I'm not asking you to give up; I'm asking you to <i>understand</i>.</span><br /> <br /> </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, I get it, really. I mean, I know that its not all that simple. Sometimes the invaders were beaten back, and sometimes they were forced to pay terrible prices. I know that some places forced the Imperial invaders to respect the natives. But the thing is, the trend is still there. I mean, look at America and Canada right now, and what happened to the native populations... Yeah, they can certainly beat them back. But it really fucking sucks for the native population. The Empires didn't crumble, not for quite some time. And only after lots of death and suffering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T03:25:57-08:00","id":1367474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367473#post1367473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was making a joke on how Lunars in 2e tend to get a bit shafted, you know, not really doing much in the game's backstory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Careful about that now; some are still really salty about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367473#post1367473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh no, I get it, really. I mean, I know that its not all that simple. Sometimes the invaders were beaten back, and sometimes they were forced to pay terrible prices. I know that some places forced the Imperial invaders to respect the natives. But the thing is, the trend is still there. I mean, look at America and Canada right now, and what happened to the native populations... Yeah, they can certainly beat them back. But it really fucking sucks for the native population. The Empires didn't crumble, not for quite some time. And only after lots of death and suffering.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a &quot;powerful individual shows up and helps a people to challenge a technologically superior empire&quot; narrative that probably feels a bit more &quot;real,&quot; I'd look at <i>Avatar: the Last Airbender</i>. Having the Avatar show up didn't make the Fire Nation crumble overnight.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T05:12:20-08:00","id":1367496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367474#post1367474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Careful about that now; some are still really salty about that.<br /> <br /> For a &quot;powerful individual shows up and helps a people to challenge a technologically superior empire&quot; narrative that probably feels a bit more &quot;real,&quot; I'd look at <i>Avatar: the Last Airbender</i>. Having the Avatar show up didn't make the Fire Nation crumble overnight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I've seen Avatar, the Last Airbender. But I don't quite think its a good fit. <br /> <br /> For one thing, the technological difference is of a lesser degree<br /> <br /> Secondly, Aang's powers are different from those of the Exalted<br /> <br /> Thirdly, there are multiple Exalted. <br /> <br /> And more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T05:21:43-08:00","id":1367500,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying it's a <i>perfect</i> fit - just that it fits <i>better </i>than Jeff Goldblum, Randy Quaid and Will Smith defeating an army of aliens in one fell swoop after getting their nuts stomped for three-quarters of the movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T05:30:55-08:00","id":1367503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1367500#post1367500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying it's a <i>perfect</i> fit - just that it fits <i>better </i>than Jeff Goldblum, Randy Quaid and Will Smith defeating an army of aliens in one fell swoop after getting their nuts stomped for three-quarters of the movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly speaking the entire thing shouldn't be a movie. It should be a TV show. <br /> <br /> More time that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T07:58:48-08:00","id":1425164,"title":"","content":"<i>\u201cThe most merciful thing in the world, I think, is the inability of the human mind to correlate all its contents. We live on a placid island of ignorance in the midst of black seas of infinity, and it was not meant that we should voyage far. The sciences, each straining in its own direction, have hitherto harmed us little; but some day the piecing together of dissociated knowledge will open up such terrifying vistas of reality, and of our frightful position therein, that we shall either go mad from the revelation or flee from the light into the peace and safety of a new dark age.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen the liberated Old Ones would teach them new ways to shout and kill and revel and enjoy themselves, and all the earth would flame with a holocaust of ecstasy and freedom.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <br /> The world has long since gone mad. No, that would be too kind a word. The universe, the multiverse, has long since gone insane. The stars have long gone right, and the Old Ones have come. Call it Case Nightmare Green. The end of the world. The End Times. Apocalypse. Rapture. It didn't matter. Mankind no longer rose on shining cities. Mankind no longer lived on the green grass, beneath the blue sky. They no longer wore clothing of cotton, of silk, of flax. They did not write, make poetry, or any other things like invention. They did not build roads, bridges, houses, nor pottery. The Old Ones have come, and mankind fell from its once lofty perch. Forget the promise of civilization. Forget things like BASILISK attacks and computational demonology or D-engines. Mankind now lived like animals, maddened, the majority of their free will compromised. They rutted, worshipped, drank, ate, and were dressed only in the most rudimentary of animal skins. They knelt at the feet of gods, the Elder Races, the Old Ones, and everything in between. Barely sapient, knowing only the mad songs of the Things Beyond. A wretched existence.<br /> <br /> Somewhere, somewhen, in the universe, the Vault of Exaltation opened. And the sun rose. The pall of madness that clouded their minds was pushed away by the burning exaltation. The slavery placed on them was torn apart. Illumination followed Exaltation. Exaltation does not care about heartiness of body, or in more desperate situations, of mind. It only needed one thing. Free Will, and the desire to change the world. And the remnants of the human race, battered and reduced as they were, had this. <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The Exalted were created for one thing and one thing alone: To fight that which cannot be fought, and come out victorious&quot; </i><br /> <br /> Warriors with rage in their hearts took to battle against their previous masters, first wielding crude stone tools, then steel swords, then titanium, then orichalcum and plasma blades. Singers, performers, dancers, put a show for their fellows. Not just to distract their enemies, but to protect the minds of their warriors against madness and control. Craftsmen whose previous magnum opus were animal skins and crude flint now cranked out holy weaponry and spaceships, with forges that far surpassed anything that they had previously. Servitor races were created. Vast vaults, filled to the brim with cloning tanks, pumped out legions of humans for population replacement. The human race from mere tens of thousands to millions, then billions, implanted with memories and skills and used to fight monsters from beyond reality, their minds ringing with propaganda and the golden words of Solar cheerleaders. <br /> <br /> The very structure of the universe buckled and broke, and at the very end, the monsters were driven back, curious and horrified at what had happened to them. Several of their number were dead. Some didn't even realize it happened, so deep within their dreaming they were, or so ignorant. Either way, now it is a cold war. A humanity, recently freed from their shackles within living memory, all of them recently empowered by the standards of canon. No more than several centuries old. Now that they have breathing room, they now have time to rebuild, take stock of themselves, and bring the fight to the old ones. <br /> <br /> Life within the territory taken by the Exalted is one fraught with uncertainty, fear, and terror. There is now a new generation of children who have never known the madness inflicted by the Ones Beyond. There are clone pilots who have exalted, or those who have not, and are now resentful of the lower status they hold as cannon fodder to slow down attacks. Servitor races now work, but not only are they agitating for rights and rebellion, but the Exalted Host is now split on what to do with them. Some call for extermination. Some call for slavery. Some call for mercy. <br /> <br /> The Exalted are now battle-scarred warriors who have seen things man was not meant to see. Yes, they have charms to protect against madness and mind control. Yes, they have charms to protect against insanity and fatigue. No, this does not mean that they are completely unharmed by the war. In the fight for all mankind, there are no civilians. Which means that even the most cloistered scholars have seen things that would have a lesser man shaken. This includes majority of the living Celestial Exalts, all Sidereals, and all elder Dragonblooded. This has led to some tensions with their younger, minor counterparts. <br /> <br /> The sudden and new freedom of humanity has done strange things. Lacking any original myth binding them together save for the coming of the Exaltations. There is no Unconquered Sun to give grand speeches on the potential of humanity. There is no Mandate of Heaven to legitimise them, or even explain what they are. There is no spirits, no gods, no greater mythology to comfort them and tell them of their place in the universe. No Jadeborn backup. No friendly autochthon. No Dragon Kings. No Yu-Shan. All in all, the Exalted are very very aware they are alone in a hostile universe, and that if they were to fail, humanity has failed forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T23:06:50-08:00","id":1425319,"title":"","content":"Why is it, when a thread is necro'ed, it is always you?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://wompampsupport.azureedge.net/fetchimage?siteId=7575&amp;v=2&amp;jpgQuality=100&amp;width=700&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fi.kym-cdn.com%2Fentries%2Ficons%2Ffacebook%2F000%2F027%2F996%2Fharry.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T23:27:15-08:00","id":1425322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1425319#post1425319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is it, when a thread is necro'ed, it is always you?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://wompampsupport.azureedge.net/fetchimage?siteId=7575&amp;v=2&amp;jpgQuality=100&amp;width=700&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fi.kym-cdn.com%2Fentries%2Ficons%2Ffacebook%2F000%2F027%2F996%2Fharry.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you don't like it I can always start up a new thread. But that would be too much effort, too much work, and too much bandwidth devoted to a small idea. <br /> <br /> And oh yes! Another thing. Think of this entire thing like post-apocalypse and battlestar galactica and Gunstar Autochthonia. Now, the Exalted don't have backup from the gods or autochthon. But they certainly have plenty of their own power. Maybe instead of lands, they instead of a gigantic starship ala Battlestar Sol. A single immense starship with a hole in space, not dissimilar to a N/A demense, capable of near infinite power, engines the size of continents and guns that entire moons can be swallowed by. With a perfect defense to boot. And probably an entire army of alchemicals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T02:06:43-08:00","id":1425332,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a mix of Tribe 8 (which is post-apoc humans where magically impowered humans rise up and drive off incomprehensible amoral alien gods) and Stargate (which is 'Murican-military-humans F**k Yeah! Fighting the evil alien 'gods' with good old fashioned military know-how! But a little bit more thoughtful and Trek-y about it than you'd expect from that...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T04:36:12-08:00","id":1425496,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> On a total tangent are you doing okay ? The last time I saw a message from you you seemed to be extremely sick. Take care of yourself","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T08:16:37-08:00","id":1425521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1425496#post1425496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> On a total tangent are you doing okay ? The last time I saw a message from you you seemed to be extremely sick. Take care of yourself</div> </div> </div> </div>I am fine and mostly alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T08:32:14-08:00","id":1425523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1343514-the-exaltations-show-up-in-other-settings?p=1425332#post1425332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a mix of Tribe 8 (which is post-apoc humans where magically impowered humans rise up and drive off incomprehensible amoral alien gods) and Stargate (which is 'Murican-military-humans F**k Yeah! Fighting the evil alien 'gods' with good old fashioned military know-how! But a little bit more thoughtful and Trek-y about it than you'd expect from that...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes... and no. <br /> <br /> there's a Humanity fuck yeah! there, almost certainly. I mean, humans were, for the first time, able to overthrow their shackles. They were able to fight that which could not be fought, and came out victorious. They looked at the abyss in the eye and spat in its face. And they, for a measure... succeeded. <br /> <br /> But they're also deeply, deeply afraid. They know they could have lost. They know what could have happened instead. And now with heightened senses they know what is out there. <br /> <br /> If this was Trek.... <br /> <br /> &quot;To explore strange new worlds.... and exploit them. To seek out new life forms and new civilizations.. and destroy them. To boldly go where no one has gone before.... and carve a dominion in it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}